WEBVTT

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:06.133
Portland City Council to order on

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.066
Tuesday,

00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:09.300
April 14th.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.667
Please stand with me if you wish to,

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:18.033
to show our respect to the multicultural republic

00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:21.000
that is the United States of America.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:25.734
I pledge allegiance to the flag of the United States of

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.467
America, and to the Republic for which it stands,

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.500
one nation, under God, indivisible, with

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.934
liberty and justice for all.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:41.266
Thank you. Mr. City Manager, may we have a roll call, please?

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.100
Oh, yes.

00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:43.934
Councilor Scott?

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:44.867
Here.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.634
Councilor Walker?

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:45.934
Here.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:46.967
Councilor Coleman?

00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:47.367
Here.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.200
Mayor Tipton?

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:49.400
I am here.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.333
Councilor Pride?

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:50.767
Here.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.734
Councilor West?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.066
Here.

00:00:52.266 --> 00:00:53.000
Councilor Matthews?

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:53.567
Yes, sir.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.767
Thank you. We're all here. We're being joined by some more guests.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.200
Maybe that will continue.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:06.700
So I just wanted to explain how this evening's going to work

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.367
so that everybody's clear. And I also want to say that it is

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:14.467
truly my privilege to be with all of you for

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:18.033
this gathering in which we are going to engage in a democratic

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.233
process. Aren't we fortunate? So thank you.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:26.300
Because we didn't get to hear it last week, we're hearing a presentation from the

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.533
schools on what is now the school board's budget.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.467
Then the councilors will likely have some questions.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:37.400
It could be that the city manager be asked to make clarifications, but

00:01:37.533 --> 00:01:40.867
mostly we will stick to councilor questions.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.700
Then we're moving to public comment, and I'll tell you about that in

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.467
one moment.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:50.667
And then the council will have a discussion.

00:01:51.266 --> 00:01:55.033
It's a workshop, so the council doesn't do any voting tonight,

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:59.467
but we'll have a discussion, and from the discussion, I

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:03.133
think it will become clear how our councilors are feeling about the school

00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:07.166
budget, and whether we'd like to offer any additional guidance on

00:02:07.266 --> 00:02:07.667
that.

00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:13.333
I wanted to read our rules of public comment,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:18.100
and remind folks that at our workshops, which

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:22.000
tonight is, we don't have an open public comment

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:25.834
period. So your comments need to be confined to

00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:29.700
items that are on our agenda for the workshop.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:34.500
Comment is three minutes. You're going to see the timer

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.233
running when you're making comments.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.834
You'll get a reminder at 30 seconds that you might want to

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.467
start wrapping up, and also,

00:02:43.266 --> 00:02:47.133
if you want to make comments that are less than three minutes long, go for it.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:53.567
The other thing I would say is we don't have clapping or booing, and we don't do

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:57.333
ceding of time to others. Each person, individual,

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:58.533
gets three minutes.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.133
So those are our rules.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.433
I was just wondering if...

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:11.533
I think there may be some clarification ahead of the

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:15.367
authorities of the school board, and the

00:03:15.433 --> 00:03:19.100
authorities of the council, and I think it's

00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:22.734
singular authority. But I think at this time,

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.900
we don't need to talk about that until we get rolling.

00:03:26.066 --> 00:03:30.033
So let's hear the budget presentation from the schools.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.767
All right. Good evening, everyone.

00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:48.033
My name is Abigail Ketchen, and I serve as the Director of Finance for the

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.533
South Portland School Department.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.734
And tonight I'm going to share with you our FY27 board budget.

00:03:56.266 --> 00:03:57.467
I'm going to give an overview,

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.233
and then I'll be turning it over to Chair DeAngelis for a board request

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:03.200
of the city.

00:04:05.266 --> 00:04:07.367
Excuse me, is Chair DeAngelis with us?

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.100
Yes.

00:04:08.433 --> 00:04:09.166
She's outside.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:10.400
She stepped out.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:11.333
Yeah.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.634
I will go down and see if I can find her.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:20.033
All right. Well, she's welcome to join at any time, but I

00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:21.700
just note her absence.

00:04:24.266 --> 00:04:27.800
All right. So I want to take you through a little bit of our before and

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.367
after.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:31.734
You can see our

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:36.367
overall budget. What I first want to direct your attention to is the

00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:40.333
initial budget, FY27. That's the column on the

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:42.233
far right-hand.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:47.400
So as we began our budget process, we began with a

00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:51.266
roll-forward budget, just all current costs rolling forward to the

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:52.834
next year. We

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:57.667
then added other costs that we deemed necessary, capital

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.667
expenses, other increases,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:04.033
and the like. And where we found

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:04.867
ourselves

00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:09.767
was at $84 million.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.667
And how that would have worked

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:18.667
out had we stayed there would've been an

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:22.700
over 21% tax increase for the school share.

00:05:24.066 --> 00:05:27.567
I think as we can all understand, that is a likely

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:28.300
untenable

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:30.367
situation.

00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:34.133
And so throughout the past few months,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:39.400
we have gone through a very difficult process,

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:41.333
a very painful process.

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:42.834
We've had

00:05:45.233 --> 00:05:46.600
many conversations

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.934
that have been very tough, and

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:54.634
we have years of context that sort of led us here,

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.600
and I'm not going to go through all of that tonight.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:01.867
But nevertheless, we've faced where we are

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.500
atAnd through an extraordinarily painful

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.300
process, we have made a decision to close

00:06:09.734 --> 00:06:12.467
one of our beloved elementary schools.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.800
And as you can imagine, that's extremely painful for many families.

00:06:18.333 --> 00:06:20.100
And we've also gone through

00:06:20.967 --> 00:06:23.033
whether to redistrict or reconfigure.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.033
And at this point, we are kind of working through what that will

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:32.000
ultimately look like. But we have paused on some of

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:32.266
our

00:06:33.967 --> 00:06:36.834
current push towards reconfiguring quickly.

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:41.967
In addition to closing a school, we are

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.266
also proposing

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:47.433
reducing our staff overall by about 12%.

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:52.367
So I think it has really taken a lot for us to get to

00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:57.066
a point where we can offer the taxpayers a 6%

00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:59.033
increase for the school share.

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:04.433
And we certainly hope that our efforts are recognized.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.300
We value all stakeholders, including all of our taxpayers,

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:11.634
and we've really gone through a lot to get here.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:18.433
And then I just also want to note, one of the reasons why it's sort

00:07:18.467 --> 00:07:21.734
of additionally painful to get to that 6% is that

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:26.166
our fund balance has been depleted over the years, and so then

00:07:26.233 --> 00:07:29.800
we no longer have that amount to buffer the

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.367
taxpayer experience.

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:36.367
To take you through some of the reductions that we faced.

00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:40.767
So we are currently, in order to get to that 6% mark,

00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:45.100
we are looking at losing 11% of our teachers,

00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:47.266
10% of our ed techs and clerks,

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.734
one principal, 14% of our service

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:55.567
folks, and 23% of our directors.

00:07:56.967 --> 00:08:00.834
And then overall, on the whole, that works out to about 12%

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.100
for staff overall.

00:08:06.367 --> 00:08:10.100
So the main update is we remain

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.367
dedicated to our mission.

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:16.967
As tough as it is, we are still a school district.

00:08:17.333 --> 00:08:18.934
We're still here for our students.

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:23.100
We still care about academic excellence and all that students

00:08:24.233 --> 00:08:27.867
will have opportunities for in the future. That's still there.

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:32.367
But we are at a point where, indeed, we are closing a school,

00:08:33.767 --> 00:08:36.834
and letting go of 12% of our staff.

00:08:38.934 --> 00:08:41.033
And with that... Oops, I'm sorry.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.834
I'd like to turn it over to our chair, DeAngelis.

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:52.934
Hello, Madam Chair.

00:08:53.233 --> 00:08:53.834
Hi there.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:55.767
Didn't get to say hello to you earlier.

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:59.433
Thank you, and hello to everybody, and thank you for having us tonight.

00:09:00.567 --> 00:09:04.300
The board took two actions last night, passed two

00:09:04.433 --> 00:09:07.166
actions, and they are in front of you.

00:09:08.166 --> 00:09:11.333
So the first is asking for the council to

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.634
approve considering increasing the school board portion of the tax

00:09:15.667 --> 00:09:19.166
increase from 6% to 7%,

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.500
and the purpose for that would be to add to contingency

00:09:23.567 --> 00:09:26.000
towards seeding the school fund balance.

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:26.734
And as

00:09:27.634 --> 00:09:29.867
Abigail Ketchen just said, we

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:34.533
have no money in reserve at this point.

00:09:35.066 --> 00:09:35.400
So

00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:40.000
this goal was in an effort to specifically help

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.567
us to begin to build our school fund balance.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.667
So that was the first. And the second action that the board took was

00:09:49.233 --> 00:09:52.867
to consider asking the city council

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:57.066
to fund snow plowing and school resource officers, and

00:09:57.166 --> 00:09:59.233
that was to the tune...

00:10:00.133 --> 00:10:03.634
We specifically passed an amount of $360,000

00:10:04.233 --> 00:10:04.900
to ask

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:08.734
for that to be used for

00:10:08.967 --> 00:10:11.734
$220 for our school resource officers and

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.000
approximately

00:10:13.867 --> 00:10:15.133
140,000.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.533
I shouldn't have said $220.

00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:21.634
$220,000 to fund our school

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:25.567
resource services and 140,000 for

00:10:25.634 --> 00:10:26.533
snow removal

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.133
for the

00:10:29.233 --> 00:10:32.367
next budget year, the 2026-27.

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:37.834
So that was the purpose, to utilize

00:10:37.934 --> 00:10:41.567
that offset to add to the contingency .

00:10:41.634 --> 00:10:45.500
The first one was to add to the... Well, let me just

00:10:45.567 --> 00:10:47.433
see here. Eventually seeding the school fund.

00:10:47.533 --> 00:10:48.967
Okay, that's the

00:10:50.467 --> 00:10:53.700
first one, considering the school portion of the tax increase from

00:10:53.934 --> 00:10:56.967
6% to 7%, and

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.367
that would be for the purpose of adding to our

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.200
contingency and eventually seeding the school fund balance.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:08.100
The second item is for the city

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:11.800
to absorb the cost for the 26-27

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.734
budget year for snow plowing at 140,000 and

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.700
school resource officers at 220,000,

00:11:20.033 --> 00:11:23.166
to the tune of 360,000. So we passed both those

00:11:24.066 --> 00:11:25.233
requests last night.

00:11:26.033 --> 00:11:28.567
And if anybody has any questions, I'm happy to answer them.

00:11:30.767 --> 00:11:31.400
Thank you.

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:39.066
Is that the end of the presentation? Okay.

00:11:39.467 --> 00:11:41.834
We're going to move to council questions in a moment.

00:11:42.166 --> 00:11:46.133
Remember, I wanted to say, because I saw quite a few folks come in,

00:11:46.266 --> 00:11:50.233
that we are going to have a public comment period after the

00:11:50.266 --> 00:11:52.367
councilors have a chance to ask questions.

00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:56.667
You probably won't be surprised to learn that it is three minutes long.

00:11:57.066 --> 00:12:00.667
You'll see timers here that show you how much time you have.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:01.533
And

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:04.600
yeah, I think that's about it.

00:12:06.367 --> 00:12:08.734
The other thing is I said we'd have some opportunities for

00:12:08.767 --> 00:12:11.467
clarification.Seeing

00:12:11.734 --> 00:12:15.533
what the school board chair just

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:19.300
presented, I saw that you had presented based

00:12:19.467 --> 00:12:23.066
on the board moving this yesterday, that the ask

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.667
for a 1% increase would be for the contingency.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.900
I just wanted to make something clear, and I'm going to make it clear by reading

00:12:30.934 --> 00:12:34.667
aloud from what we have posted. "If the council elects to

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:38.600
increase or decrease the school budget amount, it can only do so

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.567
to the bottom line number per state law and city charter.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:46.600
Council cannot dictate which specific items to add, cut,

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:50.634
increase, decrease, including whether or not a school building

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.200
is closed. Should a majority of the council opt to increase or

00:12:54.333 --> 00:12:57.934
decrease the bottom line school budget amount, the

00:12:58.033 --> 00:13:01.533
school board would then meet to discuss how it would make additional

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:05.166
cuts if decreased, or spend the additional funds if

00:13:05.266 --> 00:13:06.500
increased." So,

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.100
it is interesting to hear your school board's

00:13:11.133 --> 00:13:14.967
intention for using an extra 1%,

00:13:15.367 --> 00:13:19.200
but it is not anything that the council dictates, and so I want to

00:13:19.233 --> 00:13:20.000
make that clear.

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:22.867
All right, councilors.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:25.467
Oh, yes.

00:13:26.634 --> 00:13:28.900
Again, Rosemary DeAngelis, school board.

00:13:29.333 --> 00:13:32.934
I just wanted to say that was specific for the

00:13:33.767 --> 00:13:37.533
board, and that was specific because that was the

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.867
way to engage in discussion and to get the vote.

00:13:41.734 --> 00:13:45.667
So that was how we got to a unanimous vote, was with

00:13:45.734 --> 00:13:48.300
the commitment amongst ourselves.

00:13:48.333 --> 00:13:52.166
It was not about coming to the council for that approval, but the

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.233
commitment amongst ourselves that that's how the money would be used.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:59.100
So that's why, and we just included that before you

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.100
tonight. Thank you.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.567
Thanks very much.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:07.033
Okay, councilors, a volley of questions, or at least

00:14:07.166 --> 00:14:09.533
a few. Anyone want to go first?

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.100
Councilor Scott, thank you very much.

00:14:14.467 --> 00:14:16.333
Thank you. I'm happy to go first.

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:21.934
I think I'd like to understand between the budget,

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.433
which I think is a 6% increase, and the additional request,

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:29.834
what the actual percentage is that the school board

00:14:29.934 --> 00:14:33.800
is asking for in terms of a school board budget, and

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.967
what that tax impact is. Appreciating that there are sort of a

00:14:39.066 --> 00:14:42.834
couple of different requests in there, but I think in the end, it

00:14:42.934 --> 00:14:43.500
is sort of

00:14:45.634 --> 00:14:49.500
attributable to the school portion of our overall city budget,

00:14:49.667 --> 00:14:53.634
and would like to make sure that we, as a council, understand

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.533
those numbers, that request, and that we are

00:14:57.233 --> 00:14:58.767
approving or reviewing

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.000
sort of a single number that is ultimately attributable to the

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.700
school portion of our budgets.

00:15:08.233 --> 00:15:12.133
Hi. Thank you for the question. So for our bottom

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:16.200
line budget, we would add about 540,000, and that would lead

00:15:16.266 --> 00:15:19.567
to a tax increase from 6% to

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.133
7% for the school share.

00:15:23.767 --> 00:15:26.100
Sorry. That's inclusive of

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.500
both the six-

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:29.734
No

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:30.634
... to 7%.

00:15:30.767 --> 00:15:30.867
No.

00:15:30.967 --> 00:15:34.934
And, I guess-No, that is the... Okay. Yeah. So the two requests, the first one is to increase

00:15:34.967 --> 00:15:38.834
from 6% to 7%. For us, the dollar amount to the bottom

00:15:38.934 --> 00:15:42.900
line is about 540,000. And then we're additionally asking

00:15:43.033 --> 00:15:46.700
for the city to cover two school resource officers and snow

00:15:46.734 --> 00:15:47.166
plowing.

00:15:48.767 --> 00:15:52.667
For us, that would not impact our bottom line, but obviously it would

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:53.200
impact

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.033
the city's bottom line.

00:15:58.233 --> 00:15:59.200
Okay, to clarify-

00:15:59.367 --> 00:15:59.834
Well, actually-

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.700
Yeah, I don't see that as...

00:16:05.867 --> 00:16:06.066
If it,

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.333
quote-unquote, "Impacts the city's bottom line," I think it

00:16:11.333 --> 00:16:15.200
should be attributable to the school board portion, so therefore

00:16:15.233 --> 00:16:19.100
I'm trying to make sure that there's transparency between the

