01:41:13.634 --> 01:41:15.200
budget. Is that true?

01:41:15.367 --> 01:41:15.500
Correct.

01:41:15.867 --> 01:41:16.100
It is

01:41:16.900 --> 01:41:18.200
true that they are not.

01:41:18.600 --> 01:41:18.767
Correct.

01:41:19.100 --> 01:41:19.100
Correct.

01:41:19.200 --> 01:41:19.500
Okay.

01:41:19.567 --> 01:41:22.700
Yeah. I know that they are upcoming costs, though, and-

01:41:22.834 --> 01:41:25.567
Right. So what I'm trying to think about is,

01:41:26.300 --> 01:41:30.200
obviously, we've heard from one of the counselors and from

01:41:30.300 --> 01:41:34.266
other folks that the idea of exploring how does the

01:41:34.300 --> 01:41:38.200
city and the school in the future perhaps work together, particularly on capital

01:41:38.266 --> 01:41:41.800
expenses, sounds like that might become a workshop of the

01:41:41.867 --> 01:41:42.266
future.

01:41:44.000 --> 01:41:44.133
Okay.

01:41:44.133 --> 01:41:44.266
Okay.

01:41:44.300 --> 01:41:45.367
And I'm comfortable with that.

01:41:46.800 --> 01:41:50.700
As we're talking about this, I want to talk about what is our appetite for

01:41:50.934 --> 01:41:54.500
all possible creative solutions, and I think beyond the SROs and

01:41:54.567 --> 01:41:58.133
the plowing, I think those are other areas that we could

01:41:58.166 --> 01:42:01.934
explore how do you either share those costs, cover those costs, things like that.

01:42:02.000 --> 01:42:05.166
Because I know that that was a big concern from a facilities perspective.

01:42:05.200 --> 01:42:07.500
But Counselor Walker, I'm just clarifying.

01:42:07.600 --> 01:42:08.634
I still have way more to say.

01:42:09.166 --> 01:42:11.934
Yes. And I'm not cutting you off, but I'm clarifying.

01:42:11.967 --> 01:42:15.400
Your intention is to discuss those kinds of

01:42:15.500 --> 01:42:18.700
costs in future budget setting because

01:42:19.333 --> 01:42:22.967
how we discuss that now in time for their meeting on the

01:42:23.100 --> 01:42:26.700
29th, in time to get something back to us on the 5th, seems

01:42:26.800 --> 01:42:27.533
challenging.

01:42:27.600 --> 01:42:29.133
Okay. And if that's-

01:42:29.200 --> 01:42:31.467
But you don't have to fold. I'm just trying to clarify.

01:42:31.500 --> 01:42:35.233
Oh, I'm not. I'd like to talk about that as a

01:42:35.266 --> 01:42:39.200
council. Is that something that we would be willing to do?

01:42:39.266 --> 01:42:42.667
I understand that that might make sacrifices for other capital

01:42:42.700 --> 01:42:43.333
projects

01:42:44.467 --> 01:42:48.266
that are pending, but I think it is something that we

01:42:48.300 --> 01:42:52.033
should talk about as a community or as a council because that does impact the

01:42:52.133 --> 01:42:55.900
entire community. And it is those costs, either if they are bonded

01:42:56.300 --> 01:42:59.934
or go into the school budget, do eventually come back to the taxpayers.

01:42:59.967 --> 01:43:00.100
Mm-hmm.

01:43:00.100 --> 01:43:04.066
So it is a shell game, and I just want to talk about basically where to put the

01:43:04.066 --> 01:43:04.367
shells.

01:43:05.200 --> 01:43:05.600
Okay.

01:43:06.467 --> 01:43:07.867
Do you want to hear my other stuff first?

01:43:07.967 --> 01:43:08.800
Yes, please.

01:43:09.200 --> 01:43:09.233
Okay.

01:43:09.266 --> 01:43:10.400
Other stuff welcome.

01:43:10.934 --> 01:43:11.533
So I

01:43:13.400 --> 01:43:16.166
respect the opinions of my fellow counselors greatly.

01:43:16.834 --> 01:43:19.500
But I categorically disagree with several things.

01:43:19.967 --> 01:43:22.934
First and foremost, I think that we should strive for the best possible education

01:43:22.967 --> 01:43:26.767
that we can give our students. I think that public education is a fundamental

01:43:26.767 --> 01:43:27.900
right of our community,

01:43:28.967 --> 01:43:32.867
