01:44:00.900 --> 01:44:02.266
of our children. I really don't.

01:44:03.967 --> 01:44:05.367
Abby, I really appreciate your

01:44:06.734 --> 01:44:10.500
analogy to Artemis with the interplanetary employees and the

01:44:10.667 --> 01:44:14.467
field of administrators, because I think that's a really interesting way to look at

01:44:14.500 --> 01:44:14.900
it. I

01:44:15.734 --> 01:44:19.667
will admit that listening to the school budget meetings, I have also

01:44:19.734 --> 01:44:23.567
shared a lot of people's questions about why there wasn't more cut at an

01:44:23.600 --> 01:44:26.333
administrator level, and I think that offers a really good perspective.

01:44:26.400 --> 01:44:29.066
So it's not our role to advise. I'm not doing that.

01:44:29.133 --> 01:44:31.433
I thought that was really good, and I wanted to highlight that.

01:44:33.166 --> 01:44:37.066
I absolutely support 8%. I think you all know that I came into this asking

01:44:37.133 --> 01:44:41.000
for nine. So I think 8% is great. I think that I

01:44:41.033 --> 01:44:44.834
would really like to see some of that money go towards restoring some of the

01:44:44.900 --> 01:44:47.333
positions, especially in special education.

01:44:47.467 --> 01:44:51.300
I think that that is just paramount to ensuring the

01:44:51.367 --> 01:44:55.133
success of both our teachers and our students in the

01:44:55.233 --> 01:44:58.967
next year. And I'd also really like to see the related arts positions at

01:44:59.033 --> 01:45:02.867
the middle school come back. I think that as many people have pointed out, I

01:45:03.233 --> 01:45:06.367
remember my own middle school years, I watched my daughter's middle school years,

01:45:06.500 --> 01:45:09.734
and those are just brutal years. And I think that the

01:45:09.800 --> 01:45:13.467
most important thing we can do is lift up our students, and the

01:45:13.500 --> 01:45:17.033
related arts positions are a place that a lot of people find a lot of joy and

01:45:17.033 --> 01:45:17.700
future paths

01:45:18.567 --> 01:45:21.233
for careers in life. So I think that I'd like to see that.

01:45:22.066 --> 01:45:24.433
That's just my wish list. I know that we don't have a say in that.

01:45:25.333 --> 01:45:27.800
In terms of the SROs and the

01:45:29.533 --> 01:45:31.834
snow plowing, I am definitely open to that,

01:45:32.634 --> 01:45:35.734
especially the SROs. I'm concerned about snow plowing, just because I

01:45:36.033 --> 01:45:39.667
know that our public works department runs pretty darn lean,

01:45:40.367 --> 01:45:43.834
and so I don't know what kind of hidden

01:45:43.934 --> 01:45:47.834
costs or consequences there could be from a staffing perspective on that.

01:45:48.433 --> 01:45:48.600
But again-

01:45:48.667 --> 01:45:50.834
We have Melissa. We have our public works director here, if you want

01:45:51.433 --> 01:45:52.867
any...

01:45:52.967 --> 01:45:56.266
I do have a-- Could I get a clarification on what you're asking?

01:45:57.300 --> 01:46:00.967
They're asking for us just to pay, not for us to do the

01:46:01.100 --> 01:46:01.400
work.

01:46:01.433 --> 01:46:01.433
Oh, okay.

01:46:01.467 --> 01:46:02.433
Is that correct?

01:46:03.233 --> 01:46:04.266
We talk to you.

01:46:05.867 --> 01:46:07.133
Oh. That's apples and oranges.

01:46:07.967 --> 01:46:08.300
I mean, we-

01:46:08.967 --> 01:46:09.967
Melissa, you can help answer-

01:46:10.066 --> 01:46:12.100
I'll let Melissa answer this, but I already know the answer to it.

01:46:12.200 --> 01:46:13.834
But I just want clarification.

01:46:13.867 --> 01:46:15.634
Thank you for asking, because I misunderstood that.

01:46:15.800 --> 01:46:17.300
I thought they were asking for us to take that

01:46:17.367 --> 01:46:20.300
on.

01:46:22.734 --> 01:46:23.533
Hi, Melissa.

01:46:23.867 --> 01:46:24.900
Hi, Melissa.

01:46:24.900 --> 01:46:25.467
Hi. I'm back.

01:46:25.900 --> 01:46:26.066
Yes.

01:46:26.333 --> 01:46:27.166
Just for the night, though.

01:46:27.233 --> 01:46:27.634
Just the night.

01:46:27.900 --> 01:46:29.734
Melissa Hutchins, public works director.

01:46:30.900 --> 01:46:34.767
So for us to take on snow plow, unfortunately, that would not be feasible at this

01:46:34.800 --> 01:46:38.033
time. We actually hire outside contractors to help us.

01:46:39.367 --> 01:46:42.900
So we have nine outside contractors that do Mill Creek, The

01:46:43.000 --> 01:46:46.634
Cove, the mall area, and Red Bank. We don't have enough staff

01:46:46.800 --> 01:46:48.967
to even maintain those roads.

01:46:49.767 --> 01:46:52.266
Also, we don't have the extra fleet.

01:46:52.634 --> 01:46:56.433
If you have a three-inch storm or more, you're going to have

01:46:56.467 --> 01:46:59.734
someone dedicated with a loader and an employee at the school.

01:46:59.800 --> 01:47:02.834
So each school would require someone there to constantly plow.

01:47:04.266 --> 01:47:07.967
And then right now, we run just enough to get the schools

01:47:08.000 --> 01:47:10.533
sanded and salted just before school opens.

01:47:10.634 --> 01:47:14.266
So the school has hired help. Nelson plows the

01:47:14.333 --> 01:47:16.700
schools. We come in, we sand and salt the schools.

01:47:17.834 --> 01:47:21.667
But we don't have the capacity or the equipment to be able to

01:47:21.734 --> 01:47:23.200
maintain schools.

01:47:23.367 --> 01:47:26.367
Okay. That's what I thought going into this, and that's what I thought you were

01:47:26.433 --> 01:47:28.867
asking for. So thank you for the clarification.

01:47:29.734 --> 01:47:30.066
Thank you.

01:47:31.066 --> 01:47:32.000
Thank you, Melissa.

01:47:32.934 --> 01:47:33.900
Thank you.

01:47:34.000 --> 01:47:34.734
Anything else?

01:47:35.634 --> 01:47:35.634
No.

01:47:35.700 --> 01:47:37.367
So where have you landed?

01:47:37.400 --> 01:47:38.467
So 8%, yes.

01:47:43.333 --> 01:47:43.433
I

01:47:45.200 --> 01:47:47.100
would be willing to do it for one year.

01:47:48.033 --> 01:47:51.900
But I do agree with the city manager that I would like to

01:47:51.967 --> 01:47:55.500
see the school dollars accurately reflect the school spending.

01:47:55.533 --> 01:47:59.166
But again, in the interest of as a community pulling together and

01:48:00.133 --> 01:48:01.166
assessing the crisis,

01:48:02.166 --> 01:48:03.233
I'd be willing to do it for one year.

01:48:05.333 --> 01:48:06.433
Okay. Thank you.

01:48:06.567 --> 01:48:07.433
You're welcome.

01:48:08.600 --> 01:48:10.266
Okay. Councillor West?

01:48:10.800 --> 01:48:12.066
Is it all right if I talk again?

01:48:12.333 --> 01:48:13.066
Yes, you may.

01:48:14.200 --> 01:48:16.433
Look, guys, this is what we have to face up to.

01:48:16.567 --> 01:48:20.400
They are going to end this year $2 million to $3

01:48:20.433 --> 01:48:21.934
million in the red.

01:48:23.300 --> 01:48:26.667
The issue of the 8% wasn't so they could get more people.

01:48:26.800 --> 01:48:30.734
It was so that they, because the way it's been explained to me is the city

01:48:30.834 --> 01:48:31.200
was going to

01:48:32.233 --> 01:48:36.200
use two to three million of our fund balance and then ask them

01:48:36.233 --> 01:48:39.967
to come in with a repayment plan. Here's where I am.

01:48:41.767 --> 01:48:44.533
I think we ought to just clean the slate.

01:48:44.634 --> 01:48:48.166
If they come in this year with a $2 to $3 million

01:48:48.233 --> 01:48:51.767
deficit, we just take our fund balance and we pay it, and

01:48:51.767 --> 01:48:55.634
that's it. We start fresh, and we hold them

01:48:55.667 --> 01:48:57.433
to some higher level of accountability.

01:48:57.500 --> 01:49:00.600
Because otherwise it is too mixed up.

01:49:01.433 --> 01:49:05.233
I had a reasonable approach, I thought, of saying, "Let's go to

01:49:05.333 --> 01:49:09.033
8%, give them. That'll bring in about a million that they could

01:49:09.200 --> 01:49:10.533
use to pay back some of it."

01:49:11.567 --> 01:49:14.634
Because they wouldn't hire any more teachers or do any of that good stuff that one

01:49:14.667 --> 01:49:16.433
of my colleagues thinks they could use it for.

01:49:16.734 --> 01:49:18.900
But I can see we are all over the map.

01:49:19.133 --> 01:49:22.233
I don't see how we can pull four councilors together with

01:49:22.300 --> 01:49:26.100
one approach. But we can't get away from the

01:49:26.133 --> 01:49:29.667
fact that they're in the red $2 to $3 million.

01:49:29.667 --> 01:49:30.967
And what are we going to do about it?

01:49:31.934 --> 01:49:32.800
Right. Well,

01:49:33.634 --> 01:49:36.567
good news for us is we could give all kinds of different guidance, and then the

01:49:36.634 --> 01:49:40.266
school board has to figure it out. But that might not be particularly

01:49:40.333 --> 01:49:42.934
helpful or responsible. May I ask you-

01:49:43.000 --> 01:49:44.867
Because it's our money. That's the reason why we have to figure it out.

01:49:44.967 --> 01:49:48.800
May I ask you for a clarification? When you say clean the slate, that

01:49:48.867 --> 01:49:49.233
means

01:49:50.066 --> 01:49:53.033
the deficit is met, but there is not

01:49:53.867 --> 01:49:55.266
a requirement to pay it back?

01:49:55.800 --> 01:49:56.333
That's correct.

01:49:56.433 --> 01:49:56.433
Okay.

01:49:56.867 --> 01:49:58.100
I think that's the only-

01:49:58.166 --> 01:50:01.600
Okay... feasible way to do it, givenAnd I'm not happy with it

01:50:01.667 --> 01:50:05.500
because, as everybody knows, I've been trying to have a capital

01:50:05.900 --> 01:50:09.767
building, take some of our excess funds and have a capital building

01:50:09.900 --> 01:50:12.834
fund so that we wouldn't be in the big mess we're in with all our buildings.

01:50:13.634 --> 01:50:16.066
But I just don't see any way around it this year.

01:50:16.066 --> 01:50:18.734
Are you still going to allow them the 8% or keep it at 6%?

01:50:18.734 --> 01:50:19.967
No. Okay, forget it. 10.

01:50:20.533 --> 01:50:20.533
No, she's going to-

01:50:20.567 --> 01:50:23.667
If I do that, then you have to go back to your 601, and that makes

01:50:24.567 --> 01:50:25.634
one of my colleagues happy,

01:50:26.700 --> 01:50:29.533
and hopefully it would make all the other ones happy because they don't have to

01:50:29.567 --> 01:50:33.333
repay the two to three million. I'm really trying to pull four councilors

01:50:33.400 --> 01:50:34.033
together here.

01:50:35.166 --> 01:50:37.533
What am I, chopped liver? I didn't get to say anything yet.

01:50:40.266 --> 01:50:40.800
Can I ask-

01:50:41.100 --> 01:50:41.400
Yes

01:50:41.600 --> 01:50:42.600
... a clarifying question?

01:50:42.600 --> 01:50:44.133
The pattern continues. Yes. Thank you.

01:50:44.166 --> 01:50:44.700
And I do very much-

01:50:45.000 --> 01:50:45.634
No, thank you

01:50:45.900 --> 01:50:46.133
... appreciate what you're-

01:50:46.200 --> 01:50:49.200
I am sorry, I'm not going to be Solomon on this one anyway, so...

01:50:50.033 --> 01:50:53.734
I just want to clarify. What you're saying is

01:50:53.834 --> 01:50:57.767
that the two to $3

01:50:57.800 --> 01:51:01.567
million fund balance is not a loan, but is

01:51:01.667 --> 01:51:04.700
just using our fund balance to fund the deficit,

01:51:06.100 --> 01:51:07.033
and that is not

01:51:08.433 --> 01:51:12.000
an additional percentage or two percentage beyond the

01:51:12.567 --> 01:51:13.900
6%. So you're saying-

01:51:14.533 --> 01:51:14.567
Correct

01:51:14.567 --> 01:51:15.066
... keep

01:51:15.900 --> 01:51:19.400
6%, eat the deficit with our fund

01:51:19.533 --> 01:51:20.800
balance, and move forward?

01:51:21.133 --> 01:51:21.867
Yeah. 601.

01:51:22.367 --> 01:51:22.533
Okay.

01:51:23.000 --> 01:51:23.500
601.

01:51:24.367 --> 01:51:24.533
So it would be-

01:51:24.567 --> 01:51:26.100
Thank you. No, I just want to clarify-

01:51:26.100 --> 01:51:26.233
Yes

01:51:26.333 --> 01:51:29.333
... where the percentages versus the fund balance was falling.

01:51:29.333 --> 01:51:33.266
So to just try to say it in a more articulate way, they are anticipating

01:51:33.300 --> 01:51:36.667
an FY26 deficit of $2 to $3

01:51:36.700 --> 01:51:40.700
million. When the books are closed, and they're ready to close the books

01:51:40.734 --> 01:51:44.467
on this fiscal year, we sit down, we see how much that is,

01:51:44.834 --> 01:51:48.100
we pay it out of our fund balance from our FY27.

01:51:48.634 --> 01:51:50.200
For them, they have

01:51:51.033 --> 01:51:53.700
developed a responsible budget for FY27.

01:51:54.133 --> 01:51:57.333
It's a 6.01% increase. They go forward with that,

01:51:57.967 --> 01:52:00.834
and next year we really hold their feet to the fire.

01:52:01.600 --> 01:52:03.533
We will never, never do this again.

01:52:06.100 --> 01:52:07.133
Thank you for the clarification.

01:52:07.934 --> 01:52:09.133
Now I wonder if I could get a

01:52:10.033 --> 01:52:13.967
majority vote for our consensus, because it's a workshop,

01:52:14.467 --> 01:52:16.033
from my colleagues on that approach.

01:52:17.100 --> 01:52:18.400
I don't know if you can.

01:52:19.300 --> 01:52:21.166
But can I say my thing now?

01:52:22.433 --> 01:52:23.567
You're the mayor, go ahead.

01:52:23.667 --> 01:52:26.166
I know. I know, but I wait until you finish.

01:52:26.200 --> 01:52:28.934
Did we hear from Councilor Matthews? I must have missed it.

01:52:29.100 --> 01:52:31.734
True. He asked questions and never really gave a position.

01:52:31.834 --> 01:52:33.767
No, I thought he landed it.

01:52:34.333 --> 01:52:34.400
No.

01:52:34.433 --> 01:52:35.834
You stuck your landing, didn't you?

01:52:35.834 --> 01:52:36.533
You can go ahead.

01:52:36.834 --> 01:52:39.033
No. Well, go ahead. Go ahead, Councilor Matthews.

01:52:39.100 --> 01:52:39.133
I

01:52:41.934 --> 01:52:45.800
personally do not feel 8% will pass.

01:52:46.133 --> 01:52:49.033
Last year there was a movement with the school vote. Okay?

01:52:49.133 --> 01:52:53.033
We normally had 5 or 600, 700, 800 tops vote.

01:52:53.100 --> 01:52:54.300
Last year we had over

01:52:55.467 --> 01:52:55.934
2,000.

01:52:56.333 --> 01:52:56.467
Yeah.

01:52:56.800 --> 01:52:59.467
2,000, and it was

01:53:00.600 --> 01:53:03.500
a significant amount of people voted against the school budget, correct?

01:53:04.133 --> 01:53:04.400
Yes.

01:53:05.200 --> 01:53:08.166
The only thing I can say is, should the city council

01:53:08.734 --> 01:53:09.867
decide to...

01:53:12.200 --> 01:53:12.467
I would

01:53:13.567 --> 01:53:15.000
move forward with 8%.

01:53:15.934 --> 01:53:19.133
You guys better get out there and preach to the choir, because I'll tell you right

01:53:19.200 --> 01:53:22.700
now, you better get all those school parents out there voting.

01:53:22.800 --> 01:53:26.533
You better get everybody out there, because the other half is coming full force, I

01:53:26.634 --> 01:53:30.400
guarantee it. And they came full force last year and almost

01:53:30.433 --> 01:53:33.700
took you. And it's going to be a long summer for the school board,

01:53:34.400 --> 01:53:38.367
a very long summer, because you guys are going to keep going back and back

01:53:38.400 --> 01:53:41.634
and back to workshops. Now, I have to say

01:53:41.667 --> 01:53:42.634
that

01:53:44.300 --> 01:53:46.734
I don't like increasing taxes on people, but I

01:53:48.033 --> 01:53:49.900
would rather do what Councilor...

01:53:52.100 --> 01:53:52.400
West.

01:53:52.467 --> 01:53:52.467
West.

01:53:52.500 --> 01:53:53.734
What's your name? Thank

01:53:55.600 --> 01:53:57.300
you. I'm on a lot of meds.

01:53:58.834 --> 01:53:59.433
So listen,

01:54:00.333 --> 01:54:04.300
I'm not a fan of that, just so you know.

01:54:04.333 --> 01:54:04.467
Oh, I know.

01:54:04.800 --> 01:54:08.467
But it doesn't raise taxes, but it doesn't allow us...

01:54:08.834 --> 01:54:12.433
It cuts us $2 million short of projects, and I just-

01:54:12.800 --> 01:54:13.033
I know

01:54:13.233 --> 01:54:16.667
... I just got a nasty letter from

01:54:16.800 --> 01:54:20.600
residents on the golf course whose houses were being pelted

01:54:20.634 --> 01:54:22.834
by golf balls because we haven't put up a net yet.

01:54:22.934 --> 01:54:23.500
Mm-hmm. Yep.

01:54:23.600 --> 01:54:25.667
So I'm

01:54:28.233 --> 01:54:31.000
really undecided at this point. I really am.

01:54:31.100 --> 01:54:31.100
It's okay.

01:54:31.100 --> 01:54:34.500
And we don't have to make a decision tonight, but I got your guidance so far.

01:54:34.567 --> 01:54:35.367
I hear you guys, so.

01:54:35.400 --> 01:54:36.967
All right. I think maybe-

01:54:37.033 --> 01:54:38.000
Go ahead. Your turn.

01:54:38.100 --> 01:54:41.734
Maybe I haven't allowed enough quick

01:54:41.900 --> 01:54:45.300
opportunity for other councilors to respond to the idea that

01:54:45.367 --> 01:54:49.300
the F26 deficit would be paid by the city

01:54:49.367 --> 01:54:53.066
in its entirety with no expectation of paying

01:54:53.133 --> 01:54:56.834
back. Does anyone want to react to that fairly quickly?

01:54:57.834 --> 01:55:00.100
I know finance director might have something to say too, if you'd like.

01:55:00.066 --> 01:55:02.934
The finance director wants to react to that.

01:55:03.033 --> 01:55:03.900
Just in general.

01:55:04.333 --> 01:55:07.133
It's generally in here. I'm not clear about the money.

01:55:07.500 --> 01:55:09.400
It's just we have going to pay our bills.

01:55:09.934 --> 01:55:10.166
Right.

01:55:12.300 --> 01:55:14.300
Ellen Samboin, finance director for the city.

01:55:17.533 --> 01:55:21.100
If we choose to draw $2 to 3 million from our fund balance with

01:55:21.166 --> 01:55:25.133
no restoration plan or no documentation of

01:55:25.300 --> 01:55:29.200
action of either how not to do that again, even for

01:55:29.200 --> 01:55:31.634
our own use, without any plan to restore it,

01:55:33.967 --> 01:55:37.900
we are going to get questioned by rating agencies when we issue our next bonds

01:55:37.934 --> 01:55:40.333
as to, "Okay, you drew $2, $3 million.

01:55:41.233 --> 01:55:44.266
What are you going to do about that?" So whether it's a payback from the schools,

01:55:44.367 --> 01:55:46.567
whether it's another plan that we have in place,

01:55:47.900 --> 01:55:51.066
if you draw fund balance with no plan to restore it

01:55:51.967 --> 01:55:55.967
and the reason behind it is for budget deficit, they're going

01:55:55.967 --> 01:55:59.734
to question that pretty heavily, and they're going to wonder what we're doing

01:55:59.800 --> 01:56:00.934
to make sure

01:56:01.800 --> 01:56:04.900
that it doesn't happen again, and if it does, what are your action

01:56:04.967 --> 01:56:08.500
plansTo take care of it or to restore

01:56:08.567 --> 01:56:12.200
it over some fairly short time period of years.

01:56:12.266 --> 01:56:15.700
So not 10 years, but two, three, four, five years.

01:56:15.734 --> 01:56:19.467
So I just caution you, if you're going to do that, we are going to have to document

01:56:19.500 --> 01:56:23.066
something that says we're just not going to write them a check and forget about it

01:56:23.066 --> 01:56:26.867
and draw fund balance for a deficit budget situation without

01:56:26.867 --> 01:56:30.667
any recognition that that's not a

01:56:30.734 --> 01:56:32.567
good thing to do on a regular basis.

01:56:33.567 --> 01:56:35.233
Okay. Can I ask you a quick question?

01:56:35.300 --> 01:56:35.467
Yeah.

01:56:35.667 --> 01:56:37.834
Would that be true of any department in the city?

01:56:37.967 --> 01:56:39.567
Say, the fire department-

01:56:39.667 --> 01:56:39.734
I don't know

01:56:39.734 --> 01:56:43.667
... or the police department said, "Whoops, we need $3 million that we overspent."

01:56:43.700 --> 01:56:46.367
It works for any department?

01:56:46.600 --> 01:56:48.166
Only if we're taking it out of fund balance.

01:56:48.800 --> 01:56:49.467
Yeah, that's what I mean.

01:56:49.500 --> 01:56:52.567
So if we had a deficit in one department and not in another, and our overall fund

01:56:52.634 --> 01:56:54.266
balance didn't take a hit, then that wouldn't be the issue.

01:56:54.333 --> 01:56:58.200
The issue is the available funds to the city. We have a fund balance policy.

01:56:58.233 --> 01:57:01.867
Are you adhering to it? If you're drawing from it, why are you doing that,

01:57:01.967 --> 01:57:05.967
and how are you restoring it? So I don't know what'll

01:57:06.000 --> 01:57:08.300
happen in the next couple of years. I don't think any of us really do.

01:57:08.667 --> 01:57:12.367
If we take $2 to $3 million out and we take money out to

01:57:12.433 --> 01:57:16.066
use for CIP or we don't, if we happen to drop below the

01:57:16.100 --> 01:57:18.166
9%, then they're going to really get concerned.

01:57:18.266 --> 01:57:18.934
Yeah.

01:57:18.967 --> 01:57:20.467
And we all hope that doesn't happen.

01:57:20.800 --> 01:57:24.734
I'll also mention that there's two ways that the school can also restore

01:57:24.767 --> 01:57:28.066
fund balance. One, obviously, we've been talking about, is raising taxes and

01:57:28.166 --> 01:57:31.667
dedicating it to a restoration. The other one is, hopefully,

01:57:32.200 --> 01:57:36.000
with some restructuring, if you generate surpluses, obviously that goes

01:57:36.066 --> 01:57:39.834
into fund balance. So that could happen over the next few years as

01:57:39.867 --> 01:57:43.600
they restructure their budget, and they may actually have a little surplus now and

01:57:43.634 --> 01:57:45.634
then that can funnel into fund balance.

01:57:45.667 --> 01:57:45.667
So-

01:57:45.700 --> 01:57:48.066
And that is what happened in prior years, prior to the past two.

01:57:48.266 --> 01:57:48.467
Correct.

01:57:48.467 --> 01:57:49.300
They were generating surpluses.

01:57:49.367 --> 01:57:52.066
Yeah, that's how they built up fund balance to over $5 million a few years ago.

01:57:52.734 --> 01:57:54.300
Okay. Ms. Scott.

01:57:54.333 --> 01:57:55.900
Yes. Would you mind staying there for one second?

01:57:55.900 --> 01:57:56.000
Sure.

01:57:56.066 --> 01:57:57.333
Yes, Councilor Scott.

01:57:57.533 --> 01:57:58.166
Just to clarify,

01:57:59.767 --> 01:58:03.433
I don't think the school department has used city fund

01:58:03.500 --> 01:58:07.166
balance in the past. They've depleted some of their fund

01:58:07.300 --> 01:58:10.500
balance, but they have not used city to cover deficits. Is that correct?

01:58:10.767 --> 01:58:13.500
Not in my tenure. I don't know what's happened a long time ago, but right.

01:58:13.600 --> 01:58:16.066
They had over $5 million. I think you guys have seen the-

01:58:16.166 --> 01:58:16.367
Yeah

01:58:16.367 --> 01:58:19.233
... the slide that shows what the use has been over the past few years. Correct.

01:58:19.634 --> 01:58:23.367
But the city does have an obligation to fund

01:58:23.700 --> 01:58:27.467
the school deficit if there is one and there's not fund balance to cover that.

01:58:27.634 --> 01:58:31.600
I'm just trying to think about our obligation to do that and

01:58:31.700 --> 01:58:35.300
how that is managed by a repayment or

01:58:35.467 --> 01:58:37.100
bond considerations-

01:58:37.300 --> 01:58:37.300
Right... in the future.

01:58:37.400 --> 01:58:41.100
So that's a great point that probably we should clarify.

01:58:41.200 --> 01:58:44.066
So because it's a municipal school district,

01:58:44.467 --> 01:58:46.567
financially, they're a part of our general fund.

01:58:46.767 --> 01:58:46.967
Right.

01:58:47.400 --> 01:58:51.266
And even though state statute and everything else isolates school fund balance and

01:58:51.367 --> 01:58:55.266
school activities and all of that stuff, it's actually restricted in our

01:58:55.300 --> 01:58:58.700
financials for schools because it can only be used for education.

01:58:59.667 --> 01:59:03.667
The financial impact is if they don't have fund balance and they have a deficit,

01:59:03.767 --> 01:59:06.066
it's coming out of our fund balance because we're all in the same fund.

01:59:06.333 --> 01:59:06.867
Right.

01:59:06.900 --> 01:59:07.533
Yeah.

01:59:07.567 --> 01:59:07.867
Yeah.

01:59:07.900 --> 01:59:11.600
So it's not just an obligation, it financially has to happen that way.

01:59:12.000 --> 01:59:12.233
Right.

01:59:12.433 --> 01:59:12.967
Yeah.

01:59:13.000 --> 01:59:13.867
Okay. Thank you.

01:59:13.934 --> 01:59:14.066
Yep.

01:59:17.100 --> 01:59:17.834
Councilor West.

01:59:18.166 --> 01:59:21.900
I'd just point out that we have lots of money in our fund balance to do this,

01:59:22.367 --> 01:59:26.233
and that in fact, the budget on page nine, the bottom paragraph,

01:59:26.600 --> 01:59:30.300
when it talks about the use of the fund balance, and then it goes on that we

01:59:30.400 --> 01:59:31.734
have currently

01:59:33.700 --> 01:59:37.667
18.7%, and then that we would go down, we'd do this

01:59:37.700 --> 01:59:40.567
and that, and then we'd end up with 12.8%.

01:59:40.600 --> 01:59:44.333
And when I pointed out that the numbers didn't make sense in that paragraph, what I

01:59:44.367 --> 01:59:47.700
was told by the city manager is that's because kind of

01:59:47.767 --> 01:59:51.367
quietly on the side, we had set aside $3 million of our fund

01:59:51.433 --> 01:59:52.500
balance for the schools.

01:59:52.600 --> 01:59:52.900
Mm-hmm.

01:59:53.000 --> 01:59:56.800
So we have already set aside $3 million, and we still

01:59:56.900 --> 02:00:00.834
end up with 12.8% fund balance. So we have plenty

02:00:01.000 --> 02:00:02.266
of fund balance to do it.

02:00:03.433 --> 02:00:05.533
And I have one more quick question.

02:00:07.000 --> 02:00:10.500
12%, it sticks in my mind as it means

02:00:10.567 --> 02:00:13.200
something. Am I completely imagining this?

02:00:13.266 --> 02:00:16.100
Is there some guideline for not going under 12?

02:00:16.100 --> 02:00:16.367
Something-

02:00:17.000 --> 02:00:19.100
So to begin with, it's your policy.

02:00:19.200 --> 02:00:22.367
So 9% is the minimum, 12% is the maximum.

02:00:22.400 --> 02:00:22.433
Right.

02:00:22.433 --> 02:00:23.367
So you want to be in between there.

02:00:23.467 --> 02:00:23.700
Oh, okay. All right.

02:00:23.700 --> 02:00:27.000
And the policy says anything over 12% can be used-

02:00:27.066 --> 02:00:27.066
Thank you

02:00:27.066 --> 02:00:30.667
... for one-time purchases. So it's typically that amount that we

02:00:30.867 --> 02:00:34.700
look to, to use for CIP. And yes, if we're at 12.8%, you would

02:00:34.767 --> 02:00:37.834
have .8%, which is maybe about $1 million,

02:00:38.800 --> 02:00:42.667
to carry into next year for CIP, barring any other, however this year

02:00:42.700 --> 02:00:46.367
ends up, if we generate a surplus or fund balance goes up or down

02:00:47.867 --> 02:00:48.233
more.

02:00:49.567 --> 02:00:49.834
Got it.

02:00:49.834 --> 02:00:50.333
That make sense?

02:00:50.467 --> 02:00:53.233
Okay. Councilor Scott.

02:00:53.300 --> 02:00:56.867
Can I clarify? I understood the 12% to be a goal,

02:00:57.400 --> 02:01:01.233
not a maximum, and that if we are above the goal, we can use that

02:01:01.266 --> 02:01:01.467
for

02:01:02.300 --> 02:01:05.467
CIP money, but not that it's a maximum, but a goal.

02:01:05.834 --> 02:01:09.734
That 9% was the minimum and 12% was the goal, and as you get above

02:01:09.767 --> 02:01:10.900
and below 12.

02:01:11.000 --> 02:01:12.867
We're kind of saying the same thing, yes.

02:01:12.967 --> 02:01:13.000
Okay.

02:01:13.800 --> 02:01:14.400
Fine.

02:01:14.533 --> 02:01:17.867
The goal is 12. Until you get over 12, you don't want to spend any-

02:01:18.533 --> 02:01:18.533
Yes

02:01:18.533 --> 02:01:20.300
... I think is the intent of the policy.

02:01:20.400 --> 02:01:20.967
Okay. Thank you.

02:01:21.033 --> 02:01:21.867
Yeah.

02:01:23.000 --> 02:01:23.367
Thank you, Mayor.

02:01:23.467 --> 02:01:24.266
Just real quick.

02:01:24.300 --> 02:01:24.967
Yes, thank you.

02:01:25.033 --> 02:01:25.767
So

02:01:28.700 --> 02:01:32.533
by us paying that, wiping that debt away, I know it

02:01:32.600 --> 02:01:34.400
doesn't help your budget this year,

02:01:35.400 --> 02:01:35.600
right?

02:01:36.900 --> 02:01:37.300
Abigail?

02:01:38.967 --> 02:01:39.367
Correct?

02:01:40.166 --> 02:01:41.133
Yes, that does not change our FY-

02:01:41.166 --> 02:01:42.200
Okay. Can she go to the podium?

02:01:42.266 --> 02:01:43.367
Yeah, go to the podium.

02:01:45.700 --> 02:01:49.567
Yes. So, having a clean slate doesn't change our FY27 budget,

02:01:49.700 --> 02:01:53.667
but it would mean we wouldn't have to budget for that in FY28

02:01:53.867 --> 02:01:57.567
and moving forward. So if we were on a payment plan in FY28 and moving

02:01:57.700 --> 02:02:01.533
forward, that would obviously come at the cost of personnel.

02:02:03.000 --> 02:02:03.467
So it-

02:02:04.367 --> 02:02:05.233
Or a tax increase.

02:02:05.767 --> 02:02:08.500
Or a tax increase. But it would be enormously helpful.

02:02:10.634 --> 02:02:14.233
And we would accept, I think, any action plan, improvement plan

02:02:14.667 --> 02:02:14.700
Yes

02:02:14.700 --> 02:02:15.767
... that we would need to show

02:02:17.433 --> 02:02:18.767
that we're not going to do this again.

02:02:21.066 --> 02:02:21.533
Thank you.

02:02:23.667 --> 02:02:24.467
Okay. Any-

02:02:24.600 --> 02:02:24.600
Yes.

02:02:24.667 --> 02:02:26.066
Oh my goodness. Yes.

02:02:26.166 --> 02:02:26.667
I will be brief.

02:02:26.734 --> 02:02:27.333
Yeah. No.

02:02:29.467 --> 02:02:31.100
Go for it. Thank you.

02:02:31.400 --> 02:02:32.834
I can? Oh, okay.

02:02:36.800 --> 02:02:37.066
So,

02:02:40.100 --> 02:02:43.066
the mayor asked for responses to Councilor West's plan.

02:02:45.667 --> 02:02:47.233
This is really hard for me to say.

02:02:48.834 --> 02:02:52.767
I think at this point, given the dire straits we truly are in,

02:02:53.867 --> 02:02:57.567
I'm going to yes, and to this one. I would support

02:02:57.634 --> 02:02:58.433
the

02:02:59.634 --> 02:03:02.500
cleaning up of the debt. We have the fund balance.

02:03:02.500 --> 02:03:04.266
We're over the 12% goal,

02:03:05.266 --> 02:03:06.667
and we still will be even if we

02:03:07.634 --> 02:03:07.867
pay

02:03:08.867 --> 02:03:10.367
as long as it's not more than three million.

02:03:11.100 --> 02:03:12.333
I can

02:03:14.467 --> 02:03:17.700
live with 8%. I agree with Councilor Matthews that you guys got to go campaign the

02:03:17.734 --> 02:03:18.266
heck out of it.

02:03:19.166 --> 02:03:23.100
And in the end, it's not so much. I will support 8%, but if you come

02:03:23.100 --> 02:03:25.066
back to me with 6%, I will support that too.

02:03:25.133 --> 02:03:28.767
It's really up to you guys to decide what the percentage you're coming back with.

02:03:28.834 --> 02:03:32.533
But obviously, we're giving the guidance as to the total that we would

02:03:32.533 --> 02:03:33.000
support.

02:03:33.867 --> 02:03:37.500
If you guys can make it work, if you guys can fund more

02:03:40.467 --> 02:03:43.867
teachers and maybe change that, that'd be great in my

02:03:45.066 --> 02:03:47.834
personal opinion, but that's not up to me.

02:03:48.233 --> 02:03:51.667
So my guidance is that if you come back with eight or less,

02:03:52.467 --> 02:03:54.133
I will vote

02:03:54.934 --> 02:03:56.033
to pass that on to the voters.

02:04:01.300 --> 02:04:02.200
Any... Okay.

02:04:03.233 --> 02:04:06.000
No, I think that's Councilor West.

02:04:06.033 --> 02:04:09.767
Dangerously, I think what I heard is coming close to some sort of consensus.

02:04:12.467 --> 02:04:16.433
And maybe I can be persuaded. Actually, where I was going to go

02:04:16.567 --> 02:04:20.533
is, in these times, I think it is appropriate for the

02:04:20.634 --> 02:04:24.000
city to make what essentially would be a grant

02:04:25.367 --> 02:04:29.233
toward the FY26 deficit. Does it have to

02:04:29.266 --> 02:04:32.367
be two million? I was going to recommend it be one million.

02:04:32.433 --> 02:04:34.567
That would be helpful.

02:04:35.900 --> 02:04:39.834
And if that one million was coming, I was going to say

02:04:40.567 --> 02:04:44.500
I would support the 7% budget. That's what has come back

02:04:44.567 --> 02:04:44.967
to us.

02:04:46.433 --> 02:04:50.233
I don't support that the city would take on

02:04:50.333 --> 02:04:53.000
operational costs of the schools.

02:04:53.133 --> 02:04:56.834
I think I've heard more than one school board member say throughout this

02:04:56.834 --> 02:05:00.433
process, we need to show people what the real costs

02:05:00.567 --> 02:05:02.834
of running our schools are.

02:05:03.667 --> 02:05:07.367
Snow plowing is one of them. SROs. I was on the school

02:05:07.467 --> 02:05:11.333
board at a time when the decision to have an

02:05:11.433 --> 02:05:15.133
SRO, I think there are... Are there two of them right now, one at the middle

02:05:15.200 --> 02:05:18.533
school, one at the high school? That was controversial,

02:05:18.767 --> 02:05:22.233
actually. That it was argued that for some students,

02:05:23.133 --> 02:05:26.233
a uniformed officer does not represent safety.

02:05:26.467 --> 02:05:26.634
It

02:05:27.433 --> 02:05:31.266
reminds them of things that they have learned to fear, and it

02:05:31.333 --> 02:05:35.233
was a controversial decision. In Portland, they decided not to

02:05:35.300 --> 02:05:36.333
have SROs.

02:05:38.634 --> 02:05:41.934
So that is something that is a school board

02:05:42.033 --> 02:05:43.166
decision.

02:05:45.000 --> 02:05:48.967
So I guess that's what I was going to take my magic

02:05:49.033 --> 02:05:52.567
wand and say, "Let's make a grant of one million for

02:05:52.667 --> 02:05:56.433
FY26. Let's do the 7% increase that

02:05:56.533 --> 02:06:00.333
was asked for, but let's not take on operational costs."

02:06:02.367 --> 02:06:02.700
Madam.

02:06:02.967 --> 02:06:06.500
If we keep working it, I think we've got a consensus to not take on the operational

02:06:06.634 --> 02:06:07.000
costs.

02:06:07.233 --> 02:06:07.467
Yep.

02:06:07.500 --> 02:06:11.433
We can go there. I think we've got a majority to give them some

02:06:11.467 --> 02:06:15.367
kind of a grant, so maybe we can talk about how much of a grant, and then maybe we

02:06:15.400 --> 02:06:19.233
could get a majority to go with the 7%, because that's what they asked us.

02:06:19.367 --> 02:06:22.934
And I do think that we shouldn't substitute our judgment for the school board,

02:06:23.467 --> 02:06:25.200
except in very unusual cases.

02:06:26.266 --> 02:06:29.600
So they came in with seven, let's go with seven, but say, "No,

02:06:31.166 --> 02:06:34.700
we won't take on these expenses," but let's now talk about the amount of the grant

02:06:34.734 --> 02:06:35.266
that we're willing to give them for-

02:06:35.300 --> 02:06:36.834
Okay. Thank you.

02:06:37.934 --> 02:06:38.100
Back to Councilor-

02:06:38.133 --> 02:06:42.100
But what if we're giving them a grant without increasing taxes?

02:06:42.166 --> 02:06:42.333
Well,

02:06:43.834 --> 02:06:45.634
excuse me, can I have a private conversation?

02:06:48.000 --> 02:06:49.567
Wait a second, I've got to move this way.

02:06:50.266 --> 02:06:51.467
This is a committee-

02:06:51.634 --> 02:06:54.400
Ron, would you support seven that was their request?

02:06:54.767 --> 02:06:56.233
The school board requested seven.

02:06:56.266 --> 02:06:58.400
The school board, that was... Yes.

02:06:58.567 --> 02:06:59.333
Would you go with that?

02:07:01.800 --> 02:07:05.634
I said that I would approve

02:07:05.667 --> 02:07:09.000
sending it to the voters. It doesn't mean that I approve it or I would vote for it.

02:07:09.000 --> 02:07:10.667
Yeah. Would you send it to the vote?

02:07:10.700 --> 02:07:14.634
But I'm just saying that they're going to have to sell it, because I don't

02:07:14.634 --> 02:07:15.033
believe-

02:07:15.100 --> 02:07:15.100
Yeah

02:07:15.100 --> 02:07:18.600
... that the voters of South Portland can really support any more tax

02:07:18.667 --> 02:07:19.266
increases.

02:07:20.100 --> 02:07:22.166
I agree that they're going to have to sell seven.

02:07:23.100 --> 02:07:27.033
But they came to us wanting seven, so then I would hope that they could sell

02:07:27.100 --> 02:07:27.400
seven.

02:07:29.233 --> 02:07:29.567
All right.

02:07:29.667 --> 02:07:32.567
And if anybody asks me individually outside of this, and not as a...

02:07:33.266 --> 02:07:35.400
I would express my opinion about seven too.

02:07:37.133 --> 02:07:38.100
Okay. If I

02:07:38.934 --> 02:07:41.934
happened to be a school board member sitting in the audience, I think I would've

02:07:42.000 --> 02:07:44.533
heard us say things and

02:07:45.867 --> 02:07:47.033
We heard them say things.

02:07:48.000 --> 02:07:51.800
And maybe would say we have the authority to go back and

02:07:51.834 --> 02:07:55.767
discuss what we heard. That's what I would say about the

02:07:55.800 --> 02:07:59.734
percentage increase. And I think we are now going to have a

02:07:59.834 --> 02:08:02.900
brief but meaningful discussion about the

02:08:03.367 --> 02:08:06.734
idea of helping with the FY26 deficit,

02:08:07.300 --> 02:08:09.066
perhaps without strings

02:08:09.100 --> 02:08:13.000
attachedAre we having

02:08:13.000 --> 02:08:13.800
that discussion?

02:08:14.066 --> 02:08:14.500
I think we should.

02:08:14.967 --> 02:08:15.100
Yeah.

02:08:15.100 --> 02:08:15.100
Yeah.

02:08:15.166 --> 02:08:15.834
Okay.

02:08:17.000 --> 02:08:18.333
Did you want to say something?

02:08:18.634 --> 02:08:22.000
Sure. I fully support the idea. I do think that we should just wipe the slate

02:08:22.066 --> 02:08:24.300
clean. I do think that we should have very

02:08:25.634 --> 02:08:28.934
clear documentation out there for our

02:08:29.033 --> 02:08:32.867
auditors and for the public to understand what we're doing and

02:08:33.066 --> 02:08:36.467
what steps can be taken to prevent this from happening again.

02:08:38.467 --> 02:08:42.200
In the spirit of this is a community problem,

02:08:42.467 --> 02:08:44.200
I think that this is a community solution.

02:08:45.066 --> 02:08:48.367
Okay. So I hear a full, whatever the deficit is-

02:08:48.967 --> 02:08:48.967
Yep

02:08:48.967 --> 02:08:52.233
... it is paid off and it does not have to be paid back.

02:08:53.066 --> 02:08:53.467
Anyone

02:08:54.433 --> 02:08:56.900
next? Is there anyone- Yes.

02:08:56.967 --> 02:09:00.634
I agree, but I would hope that the school would be

02:09:00.667 --> 02:09:04.600
instrumental in helping us with the documentation that we would provide

02:09:04.634 --> 02:09:08.266
to auditors and to those people who are setting

02:09:08.433 --> 02:09:09.567
our bond rating.

02:09:09.734 --> 02:09:09.734
Yeah.

02:09:09.734 --> 02:09:10.767
Because it's

02:09:12.100 --> 02:09:14.166
clear there's a good reason, right?

02:09:14.367 --> 02:09:18.367
I think that our finance director said we have to explain that there's a good

02:09:18.467 --> 02:09:20.800
reason that we're doing this, and it won't be as bad.

02:09:20.834 --> 02:09:20.834
Yeah.

02:09:20.934 --> 02:09:22.333
And I think it's clear there's a good reason.

02:09:22.433 --> 02:09:26.200
Let's clarify that we are actually now talking to our

02:09:26.233 --> 02:09:30.133
city manager and our finance director, and that what the

02:09:30.133 --> 02:09:34.066
school board members are hearing may have impact on some decisions they

02:09:34.133 --> 02:09:36.734
might make about their FY27 budget.

02:09:38.734 --> 02:09:39.734
Yes, Counselor West.

02:09:41.166 --> 02:09:41.934
Well, I think

02:09:43.867 --> 02:09:47.634
they've made their decision on their budget, and they came in with 7%,

02:09:48.000 --> 02:09:49.834
and we say whether we like that or not.

02:09:49.967 --> 02:09:53.500
And then the second part is, we are willing to either wipe the slate

02:09:53.567 --> 02:09:57.467
clean or do a million. Well, I was going to ask one more

02:09:57.533 --> 02:09:58.867
clarification from the school-

02:09:58.967 --> 02:09:59.000
Please

02:09:59.000 --> 02:10:01.333
... about how much this deficit is likely to be. I'm sorry.

02:10:01.367 --> 02:10:05.066
Were you saying that the food deficit is

02:10:05.133 --> 02:10:06.934
something from even before this year?

02:10:08.066 --> 02:10:10.734
Yes. So the nutrition fund is its own fund.

02:10:11.133 --> 02:10:14.533
They also used to have their fund balance, which is now depleted,

02:10:15.233 --> 02:10:18.867
kind of at the same time as ours is. But there is about

02:10:19.033 --> 02:10:22.800
408 or so deficit in

02:10:22.834 --> 02:10:26.700
the nutrition fund from FY25. And I've built that

02:10:26.767 --> 02:10:27.700
into our

02:10:28.734 --> 02:10:31.934
current deficit as a holistic look of

02:10:32.300 --> 02:10:32.900
everything.

02:10:34.200 --> 02:10:37.767
