02:51:11.567 --> 02:51:14.233
What do you think you were doing for two weeks?

02:51:15.700 --> 02:51:16.567
Homework? Yeah.

02:51:17.767 --> 02:51:18.700
Volunteering? Yeah.

02:51:20.166 --> 02:51:23.333
So we changed that to restorative practice, where a student

02:51:25.200 --> 02:51:29.166
is held accountable. It's actually a very adult process, and they get assessed by a

02:51:29.233 --> 02:51:32.967
social worker in the school, have to take accountability for their

02:51:33.066 --> 02:51:36.100
actions, and have interventions if need be.

02:51:36.667 --> 02:51:40.500
So what was cool is we were the second school in the country, then it turned

02:51:40.567 --> 02:51:44.533
into us being in a national guidebook, for many other

02:51:44.634 --> 02:51:47.400
states have now adopted our policy.

02:51:47.467 --> 02:51:50.600
And also Ken Kunen, who's in Santiago, Chile,

02:51:51.333 --> 02:51:54.967
they have it there too, so it's an international policy that South

02:51:55.000 --> 02:51:58.333
Portland adopted. We also changed our athletic code.

02:51:58.400 --> 02:52:01.367
If you as an athlete got caught,

02:52:02.867 --> 02:52:04.967
we would kick you off the team for 14 days.

02:52:05.100 --> 02:52:08.634
Don't show up, don't come to the game, don't come to practice, you're dead to us.

02:52:08.667 --> 02:52:11.567
"It's a privilege to be a Red Riot," that's what I first heard.

02:52:11.634 --> 02:52:14.467
I was like, "All right, it's a game." But anyway.

02:52:14.567 --> 02:52:17.400
So now we use restorative practice in athletic code.

02:52:17.533 --> 02:52:21.400
Some schools nearby recently adopted our code because they

02:52:21.467 --> 02:52:25.300
had, if you got in trouble at least one time, second

02:52:25.367 --> 02:52:28.100
time, you're banned from sports all four years.

02:52:28.200 --> 02:52:28.667
Oh.

02:52:28.767 --> 02:52:32.066
Never to play again. Raise your hand if you were an athlete in high school, and

02:52:32.100 --> 02:52:35.900
that was maybe your only fun thing. Yeah, I see some hands up.

02:52:37.233 --> 02:52:40.800
I taught for 20 years the class for folks who were arrested for operating under the

02:52:40.867 --> 02:52:43.700
influence, the kids that were under 21.

02:52:44.200 --> 02:52:47.767
Many of them had been suspended from school or kicked off of

02:52:47.800 --> 02:52:51.600
athletic teams. So that's always been in my mind, if we could work on this

02:52:51.700 --> 02:52:54.100
now while we had access to young people.

02:52:54.200 --> 02:52:57.867
So I just shared that piece. And two other quick fun,

02:52:58.000 --> 02:53:01.867
great things that have evolved is, and I gave you all a

02:53:01.900 --> 02:53:05.433
problem gambling graphic novel, which I always thought sounded

02:53:05.500 --> 02:53:08.000
inappropriate, but it's like a cartoon book.

02:53:09.233 --> 02:53:11.367
Four of our students are the characters in this.

02:53:11.467 --> 02:53:15.233
Did you know that problem gambling sometimes starts at age 10?

02:53:15.233 --> 02:53:18.467
And it's connected to substance use and suicide.

02:53:19.266 --> 02:53:22.734
And the teacher across the hall from me, her husband worked at Oxford

02:53:22.767 --> 02:53:26.033
Casinos, and someone hung themselves while he was working.

02:53:26.100 --> 02:53:27.333
He was a security guard.

02:53:28.367 --> 02:53:30.000
So it's serious. It starts at a young age.

02:53:30.233 --> 02:53:32.400
Four of our students are the characters in this book.

02:53:32.734 --> 02:53:36.367
It's now in 27 states and comes with a health class

02:53:36.467 --> 02:53:39.100
curriculum. Again, this is not what we had planned.

02:53:39.133 --> 02:53:41.100
We were just like, "Yeah, let's do this book.

02:53:41.166 --> 02:53:41.767
That'll be cool."

02:53:42.834 --> 02:53:45.667
And then two last things. I lied, there's two more.

02:53:46.300 --> 02:53:49.567
The other thing is we have a lot of athletes that are part of SoPo Unite.

02:53:50.066 --> 02:53:53.467
And years ago we asked them, "Hey, Josh, you're a captain.

02:53:53.500 --> 02:53:54.767
What kind of training do you get?"

02:53:55.567 --> 02:53:57.734
And he looked at us like he's looking at us now.

02:53:58.634 --> 02:54:00.100
"What are you talking about?" Like,

02:54:01.300 --> 02:54:04.800
"No training?" So Officer Gray, who was our school resource

02:54:04.900 --> 02:54:06.300
officer at the time,

02:54:07.266 --> 02:54:11.100
and a couple of other colleagues, we created a captain's training that was for

02:54:11.166 --> 02:54:14.967
every season, and it was an hour long, and we had alumni

02:54:15.066 --> 02:54:18.533
captains come back and talk about their experiences,

02:54:19.033 --> 02:54:20.634
and we did that for three years.

02:54:21.600 --> 02:54:24.734
And one of our students who-- Sometimes captains are a captain more than once.

02:54:25.433 --> 02:54:29.400
And this one guy told me, "I almost fell asleep that

02:54:29.467 --> 02:54:32.400
last time." Because he'd been through it a couple times.

02:54:32.934 --> 02:54:36.100
So now Sarah Jorgensen, who's here, is our youth consultant.

02:54:36.700 --> 02:54:40.400
She and others, with Officer Gray and others, created a

02:54:40.500 --> 02:54:44.400
nine-session leadership academy for athletes this year.

02:54:44.500 --> 02:54:47.700
We've already completed eight of the sessions, and we have college and

02:54:47.734 --> 02:54:50.967
university coaches come and speak to them.

02:54:51.100 --> 02:54:54.233
They learn about mental health, nutrition, all those great things.

02:54:54.333 --> 02:54:54.500
So,

02:54:55.400 --> 02:54:58.867
I'll leave you with this, and Sarah's going to pass it out to you, is another

02:54:58.900 --> 02:55:00.900
testimony from a statewide agency.

02:55:01.500 --> 02:55:02.400
And some of you

02:55:03.500 --> 02:55:07.066
came to a meeting two years ago with our students who wanted to

02:55:07.133 --> 02:55:10.300
improve transportation in South Portland.

02:55:10.600 --> 02:55:14.100
And you might wonder, well, what does transportation have to do with substance use

02:55:14.200 --> 02:55:18.166
prevention? Well, if you can't get to all the great places in South

02:55:18.200 --> 02:55:18.700
Portland,

02:55:19.767 --> 02:55:23.467
thank you, sorry, it's not that great if you can't get there.

02:55:23.567 --> 02:55:25.667
So our students created

02:55:27.033 --> 02:55:30.567
a map of South Portland, and we had an art contest,

02:55:31.066 --> 02:55:34.967
and it's going to be made into huge posters into the middle school, Red

02:55:35.033 --> 02:55:38.867
Bank Community Center, so that students know how to take the bus

02:55:39.300 --> 02:55:43.266
or how long it might take you to ride your bike over to Wainwright,

02:55:43.367 --> 02:55:44.567
which has a cool picture.

02:55:45.400 --> 02:55:49.266
So I'll just leave you with that this work has a

02:55:49.300 --> 02:55:53.266
ripple effect, and unfortunately, with substance use, the

02:55:53.300 --> 02:55:57.266
work is never done. I wish I could say, like, by Friday, there will be

02:55:57.300 --> 02:56:00.300
no more youth substance use. I can retire.

02:56:01.233 --> 02:56:03.900
There will always be a need to do prevention.

02:56:03.934 --> 02:56:07.333
And the more prevention you do, the less treatment and

02:56:07.700 --> 02:56:10.066
recovery resources you need to provide.

02:56:10.700 --> 02:56:11.767
So thank you, guys.

02:56:12.567 --> 02:56:13.200
I'll shut up.

02:56:13.400 --> 02:56:16.700
Thank you. No, that was fascinating. Thank you so much.

02:56:19.033 --> 02:56:21.800
So an invaluable program, fully supported.

02:56:22.333 --> 02:56:23.433
90%

02:56:24.800 --> 02:56:27.300
of all addiction start at 18. 90%.

02:56:27.900 --> 02:56:29.166
Hm. Big number.

02:56:29.300 --> 02:56:30.834
She told me that, and I almost fell on the floor.

02:56:31.333 --> 02:56:31.333
Wow.

02:56:31.400 --> 02:56:34.834
Everybody loves her. We love her. This program is invaluable.

02:56:34.867 --> 02:56:37.767
This is about prevention and proactivity,

02:56:38.834 --> 02:56:42.333
and it's far easier and cheaper to

02:56:42.634 --> 02:56:46.333
treat people and try to keep them from becoming addicted

02:56:46.433 --> 02:56:49.500
to treating them in addiction protocols

02:56:52.734 --> 02:56:56.600
Thank you for coming and sitting and spending the time, and thank you to

02:56:56.700 --> 02:57:00.567
Detective Gray for being probably the best SRO in Maine.

02:57:01.800 --> 02:57:02.200
I'm ready.

02:57:04.133 --> 02:57:04.934
Okay.

02:57:06.967 --> 02:57:07.967
