I think we're at the right

03:04:47.367 --> 03:04:49.934
place for our fines right now, 50 and 150.

03:04:50.000 --> 03:04:52.100
I think those are in line with area places.

03:04:52.734 --> 03:04:53.367
Okay. Thank you.

03:04:55.533 --> 03:04:55.533
Okay.

03:04:55.533 --> 03:04:57.266
Other councilors with questions? No.

03:04:57.300 --> 03:05:01.033
I just want one clarifying. Did you say that we have three

03:05:02.000 --> 03:05:03.934
liaison positions or two?

03:05:04.100 --> 03:05:04.433
No, two.

03:05:04.867 --> 03:05:05.367
Okay, thanks.

03:05:05.433 --> 03:05:06.867
And one is currently vacant.

03:05:07.500 --> 03:05:09.567
Oh, one's currently vacant. Oh, I thought you said two.

03:05:09.767 --> 03:05:09.767
Yeah.

03:05:09.767 --> 03:05:11.467
That's where I got confused. Okay, thanks.

03:05:12.767 --> 03:05:15.100
All right, Carter. I mean, Councilor Scott.

03:05:15.133 --> 03:05:16.900
It's fine. Councilor Carter, I like that.

03:05:18.333 --> 03:05:22.266
This is sort of a broad question across several departments, but I just noticed

03:05:22.333 --> 03:05:22.500
the

03:05:23.333 --> 03:05:27.200
sort of salary and overtime and hourly expenses seem

03:05:29.767 --> 03:05:33.367
very different, and I wonder if there's sort of an analysis

03:05:33.467 --> 03:05:36.300
of savings in terms of bringing hourly

03:05:36.967 --> 03:05:40.934
employees into a salary position, if that saves time in terms of hourly and

03:05:41.033 --> 03:05:44.634
overtime. And again, I'm the new kid on the block.

03:05:44.667 --> 03:05:44.900
Sure.

03:05:44.967 --> 03:05:46.800
But for now, I can only claim that for a little bit longer.

03:05:46.867 --> 03:05:46.867
Sure.

03:05:46.867 --> 03:05:48.500
But just trying to understand that-

03:05:48.600 --> 03:05:50.367
I used to be the new person, too. I loved that one.

03:05:52.100 --> 03:05:55.634
So we only have two salary positions, the deputy chief and myself, and everything

03:05:55.700 --> 03:05:58.367
else is by union contract. So it's all hourly.

03:05:58.867 --> 03:05:59.133
Okay.

03:06:01.767 --> 03:06:02.100
Okay.

03:06:02.266 --> 03:06:02.500
Thank you.

03:06:03.000 --> 03:06:05.834
Thank you. Anyone else, questions? All right.

03:06:06.567 --> 03:06:10.000
We're going to open public comment on the police

03:06:10.033 --> 03:06:11.233
department budget.

03:06:14.500 --> 03:06:16.834
Come on down. We'd like to hear your name.

03:06:16.934 --> 03:06:19.233
You can state the street that you live on if you'd like to.

03:06:19.433 --> 03:06:20.367
Awesome. Sounds good.

03:06:21.166 --> 03:06:22.667
Good evening, members of city council.

03:06:23.266 --> 03:06:26.934
My name is Alex Potter, and I am a new South Portland resident

03:06:27.066 --> 03:06:28.166
on Sandy Hill Road.

03:06:29.567 --> 03:06:33.233
I became a resident of South Portland just October of last year.

03:06:34.967 --> 03:06:37.900
Listening to the difficult discussions tonight regarding the school budget, I want

03:06:37.934 --> 03:06:41.800
to start by saying that I moved here with my wife, we're expecting our first child

03:06:41.834 --> 03:06:44.967
in a couple of weeks, specifically to start a family

03:06:45.033 --> 03:06:49.000
because we heard that the schools here

03:06:49.100 --> 03:06:53.066
are so good, that the community is so good for raising a

03:06:53.166 --> 03:06:56.967
family in. So thank you guys for the hard work that this community has put together

03:06:57.066 --> 03:06:58.433
to make that happen.

03:07:01.266 --> 03:07:04.367
I'm also a former Army infantry officer, West Point graduate,

03:07:05.433 --> 03:07:09.400
a former Army Ranger, and a veteran of deployments to Afghanistan, Iraq, and Syria.

03:07:11.734 --> 03:07:13.967
This is relevant because I know what it takes to secure a nation.

03:07:14.333 --> 03:07:16.066
I know what it takes to deal with bad actors.

03:07:17.133 --> 03:07:19.800
I have a profound respect for the law enforcement officers here tonight

03:07:22.133 --> 03:07:25.834
who work hard to protect this community and who might see this

03:07:25.867 --> 03:07:29.834
technology, which is AOPR, which is, I'm sure, what everyone's expecting to

03:07:29.867 --> 03:07:32.000
discuss tonight. They see that as a benefit.

03:07:32.266 --> 03:07:35.934
And I also understand that we have had that in vehicles for 15 years, and we have

03:07:36.000 --> 03:07:37.100
seven cameras already.

03:07:37.300 --> 03:07:38.634
Excuse me. You have to talk to the mic.

03:07:38.667 --> 03:07:40.033
Oh, got it. Sorry.

03:07:40.467 --> 03:07:40.567
Okay, thanks.

03:07:41.133 --> 03:07:42.934
Yep, we've had the

03:07:44.467 --> 03:07:48.367
ones in the vehicles for 15

03:07:48.400 --> 03:07:50.300
years, and we have seven already.

03:07:52.033 --> 03:07:55.967
I still think that the world has changed with artificial intelligence and

03:07:56.000 --> 03:07:57.033
the ability to

03:07:59.634 --> 03:08:00.934
actually use all of this data.

03:08:01.834 --> 03:08:05.767
Back when I was deployed, we could get hundreds of thousands of terabytes of

03:08:05.767 --> 03:08:09.467
data. But if you can't process it, then it doesn't really matter. Now we can.

03:08:10.233 --> 03:08:11.767
So this is a fundamental shift.

03:08:16.834 --> 03:08:20.133
Benjamin Franklin famously warned that those who would give up essential liberty to

03:08:20.233 --> 03:08:23.200
purchase a little temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety.

03:08:23.634 --> 03:08:26.934
We are a nation built on that exact principle, codified in our Constitution and our

03:08:26.967 --> 03:08:27.567
Fourth Amendment.

03:08:28.433 --> 03:08:31.867
These cameras flip bedrock presumption of innocent until proven guilty

03:08:31.867 --> 03:08:35.567
entirely. They subject every single citizen to a digital dragnet,

03:08:36.200 --> 03:08:39.433
tracking our vehicles and our movements using artificial intelligence to establish

03:08:39.467 --> 03:08:42.333
our daily baselines just in case we commit a crime.

03:08:43.400 --> 03:08:45.600
Technology like this will inevitably be abused.

03:08:46.266 --> 03:08:49.500
I saw firsthand in Syria what happens when authorities gain access to unchecked

03:08:49.567 --> 03:08:53.400
surveillance. There are always people who enjoy having that kind of power over

03:08:53.467 --> 03:08:57.367
others, and corruption naturally followsYou can write all

03:08:57.400 --> 03:08:58.934
the local checks and balances you want-

03:08:59.033 --> 03:08:59.400
30 seconds

03:08:59.400 --> 03:09:01.000
... this data enters a

03:09:02.367 --> 03:09:05.200
network accessible across a massive variety of agencies.

03:09:06.200 --> 03:09:09.600
We may trust our local police, but this is going to the federal level if there's a

03:09:09.667 --> 03:09:10.233
flock camera.

03:09:11.133 --> 03:09:14.233
Once we feed local data into the federal system, we lose control here in South

03:09:14.300 --> 03:09:16.300
Portland, where local governance actually matters.

03:09:17.467 --> 03:09:19.333
We also have to think beyond the immediate moment.

03:09:20.333 --> 03:09:22.667
The political pendulum of the United States always swings.

03:09:22.800 --> 03:09:26.500
If you're a supporter of the current administration, think if the other side has

03:09:26.634 --> 03:09:29.266
this power. If you're not a supporter of this current administration-

03:09:29.400 --> 03:09:29.533
Time

03:09:29.533 --> 03:09:30.900
... I don't think I have to say anything else.

03:09:32.000 --> 03:09:32.700
Good timing, I guess.

03:09:33.500 --> 03:09:35.066
Thank you. Well done. Thank you very

03:09:35.166 --> 03:09:39.000
much.

03:09:40.500 --> 03:09:43.467
I'd like to talk about...

03:09:44.300 --> 03:09:45.266
Let's see. The-

03:09:45.767 --> 03:09:46.867
Could you please say your name?

03:09:46.967 --> 03:09:49.066
Yeah. My name is Wayne Broderick, live on Union Street.

03:09:50.000 --> 03:09:50.467
And in

03:09:52.200 --> 03:09:56.000
about October 31, Sanford last year was going through quite an ordeal on these

03:09:56.033 --> 03:09:59.800
flock cameras. You guys must be aware of it, that the city council was kind of

03:09:59.834 --> 03:10:02.867
flip-flopping and eventually went with what the citizens said because they were

03:10:02.900 --> 03:10:05.033
very concerned. At the same time,

03:10:06.133 --> 03:10:09.867
about a week later, November 10th, there was a flock camera installed in South

03:10:09.934 --> 03:10:13.233
Portland down at Cash Corner. I had messaged Jessica, and she didn't really know

03:10:14.166 --> 03:10:14.967
much about it, and I

03:10:16.233 --> 03:10:17.900
did get to find out a little bit about it.

03:10:18.600 --> 03:10:22.400
It turns out that instead of messaging, like putting something on the

03:10:22.467 --> 03:10:26.066
council website or announcing this awesome new technology that we're going to get,

03:10:26.100 --> 03:10:27.400
it was just

03:10:28.433 --> 03:10:31.800
nothing. I mean, why wasn't there something on the

03:10:32.500 --> 03:10:34.800
page? I had to email. It should've been announced.

03:10:34.867 --> 03:10:38.266
There should've been some kind of transparency rather than this kind of silent

03:10:38.400 --> 03:10:41.767
rollout. So from the very beginning of this implementation, it's been

03:10:42.734 --> 03:10:46.400
kind of covert, maybe hoping people didn't understand.

03:10:46.700 --> 03:10:50.367
I remember one of the councilors mentioned to me about the budget and that it

03:10:50.400 --> 03:10:54.166
was funded through a grant. Well, that's what they're doing, is they're giving

03:10:54.166 --> 03:10:57.367
these grants to get these cameras so that it doesn't go through any budget.

03:10:57.734 --> 03:10:59.200
It doesn't get approval from the councilors.

03:10:59.200 --> 03:11:01.066
You guys may not have even known that it went up.

03:11:01.667 --> 03:11:05.467
And this flock company, those cameras can do a lot more

03:11:05.767 --> 03:11:09.567
than just license plate readers. They take photos of the people in the vehicle.

03:11:10.000 --> 03:11:13.166
They take photos of what the vehicle's got in the pickup truck bed or whatever.

03:11:15.767 --> 03:11:19.600
One person in another city was tracked 525

03:11:19.667 --> 03:11:21.367
times in a month on these cameras.

03:11:22.767 --> 03:11:26.634
And you have to remember, Edward Snowden in 2013 had told

03:11:26.700 --> 03:11:30.600
us about some of these violations that the NSA was doing, and this

03:11:30.667 --> 03:11:30.867
is

03:11:31.767 --> 03:11:35.400
bound to be abused. It's already been abused if you look up the lawsuits.

03:11:35.500 --> 03:11:39.367
Other cities have taken these cameras right out because they're just not...

03:11:40.400 --> 03:11:43.967
Some of them because they were deemed to be accessible to the public.

03:11:44.000 --> 03:11:46.066
They didn't want them to have it anymore.

03:11:46.800 --> 03:11:47.000
And

03:11:47.867 --> 03:11:51.500
it's borderline unconstitutional because it does create a digital

03:11:51.533 --> 03:11:54.000
dragnet of everybody, whether or not you've done anything wrong.

03:11:56.000 --> 03:11:56.133
The

03:11:58.333 --> 03:12:02.266
information isn't held locally. It's held in these national servers, and these

03:12:02.300 --> 03:12:06.200
companies aren't really... They're into profit, so they're going to try to

03:12:06.200 --> 03:12:09.300
sell your data to other companies. They're going to cooperate with ICE.

03:12:09.700 --> 03:12:13.400
So by allowing these cameras, you're essentially feeding that information to ICE.

03:12:13.400 --> 03:12:13.767
30 seconds.

03:12:16.266 --> 03:12:16.400
And

03:12:17.233 --> 03:12:17.800
it's just

03:12:18.867 --> 03:12:22.867
to not have transparency at the beginning, I think, is what bothers me the most

03:12:23.000 --> 03:12:26.800
because you can say, "Well, we're going to be whatever." But the rollout,

03:12:26.900 --> 03:12:30.500
especially considering everything that was going on in Sanford, to just do it

03:12:30.600 --> 03:12:32.567
silently seems to be in poor taste.

03:12:32.600 --> 03:12:36.567
And I don't think you guys had all the information about it or maybe didn't share

03:12:36.600 --> 03:12:37.667
that you knew because

03:12:38.500 --> 03:12:42.033
it just was not a very transparent rollout like we'd expect to see with law

03:12:42.066 --> 03:12:42.600
enforcement.

03:12:42.800 --> 03:12:43.066
Time.

03:12:44.100 --> 03:12:45.367
Thank you very much.

03:12:46.734 --> 03:12:49.867
Keep them coming, folks, if you're here for commenting.

03:12:51.634 --> 03:12:53.900
Hi, everybody. Alex Redfield on Cooper Street.

03:12:54.867 --> 03:12:58.600
Thank you to the council, Mr. Morelli, Mayor Tipton,

03:12:58.767 --> 03:13:02.600
and all of the city staff and leaders who put a lot of

03:13:02.634 --> 03:13:06.033
work into this meeting, this budget, and making the city a place I'm

03:13:06.100 --> 03:13:08.900
happy to live in and raise my kids in.

03:13:09.000 --> 03:13:12.567
I have been to more city council meetings than usual recently, and I've tried a few

03:13:12.600 --> 03:13:14.634
different approaches to help my comments land.

03:13:14.800 --> 03:13:17.266
Tonight, I'm going to try authenticity.

03:13:18.266 --> 03:13:21.333
I took a second to check in with my six-year-old about what I've been doing for the

03:13:21.367 --> 03:13:25.266
last two Tuesdays. I told her the city is coming together to figure out what

03:13:25.300 --> 03:13:28.467
to spend money on next year, that there's not quite enough to do everything for

03:13:28.467 --> 03:13:31.567
everyone right now, and everyone's trying to figure out what's most important.

03:13:32.300 --> 03:13:34.066
She told me the answer to that question.

03:13:34.166 --> 03:13:37.166
She said the most important thing is that there is a new swimming pool with open

03:13:37.266 --> 03:13:39.533
swim after 3:00 that I can go to after school.

03:13:39.667 --> 03:13:41.800
So if you can make that happen, that would be really helpful.

03:13:42.567 --> 03:13:46.266
I chose not to bring up with her the issue that I'm here to speak about tonight,

03:13:46.333 --> 03:13:50.266
the police department's contract with Flock Safety, because I don't really know

03:13:50.333 --> 03:13:52.166
how to do it in a way that I feel good about.

03:13:52.567 --> 03:13:56.433
I can't quite figure out how to say that there are cameras out there that know

03:13:56.467 --> 03:14:00.266
when we go to the trampoline gym, and that the police use those cameras to

03:14:00.300 --> 03:14:04.166
find bad guys, but that other police outside of South Portland have

03:14:04.233 --> 03:14:07.700
used those same cameras to do awful things to good people who have done nothing

03:14:07.700 --> 03:14:11.300
wrong. I'm not ready to take on that conversation about how

03:14:11.634 --> 03:14:15.500
and why we would prioritize this over any number of essential projects

03:14:15.500 --> 03:14:19.300
and costs that truly build a better, safer community, let alone a new

03:14:19.367 --> 03:14:19.800
swimming pool.

03:14:20.800 --> 03:14:24.467
So I'm asking for your help in making sure that we can all talk about this and feel

03:14:24.533 --> 03:14:28.133
good as we do so. If you, as stewards of the city and the

03:14:28.166 --> 03:14:32.000
institutions within it, can confidently say that our relationship with

03:14:32.066 --> 03:14:35.400
Flock is fundamentally different than the relationship between the Mountain View,

03:14:35.433 --> 03:14:38.967
California, Police Department, where Flock recently was

03:14:39.033 --> 03:14:42.700
revealed to have enabled a nationwide sharing setting without local authorization,

03:14:42.834 --> 03:14:46.567
that would help me feel better. If you can learn why the hits on South

03:14:46.634 --> 03:14:50.533
Portland cameras come up 1,200 times in the haveibeenflocked.com public

03:14:50.567 --> 03:14:54.500
database of audit logs released from police departments in Texas and Georgia

03:14:54.600 --> 03:14:57.834
that have signed 287G agreements with federal immigration

03:14:57.900 --> 03:15:00.133
agencies, that would help me, too.

03:15:00.166 --> 03:15:03.700
And until you have that certainty and confidence and can help communicate that to

03:15:03.700 --> 03:15:06.767
the growing number of citizens who are concerned about this decision and its

03:15:06.800 --> 03:15:10.734
impact, I'd urge you to heed the guidance offered by Pedro Vazquez on

03:15:10.767 --> 03:15:12.634
behalf of the Human Rights Commission last week.

03:15:13.066 --> 03:15:16.867
And to paraphrase, that guidance was to recognize that this continuing partnership

03:15:16.867 --> 03:15:20.734
with this company creates risk at best and harm at worst to the segments

03:15:20.800 --> 03:15:24.767
of our community that are most in need of rebuilding trust at this moment.In

03:15:24.834 --> 03:15:28.266
summary, please park this. Help everyone dig into issues at play

03:15:28.333 --> 03:15:32.266
here. Bust out the fine-tooth comb, or I guess, yeah, as

03:15:32.300 --> 03:15:36.166
Councilor Matthew said earlier, let's take the time to dive deep to ensure

03:15:36.200 --> 03:15:38.500
that our spending commitments across all departments-

03:15:38.667 --> 03:15:38.900
30 seconds

03:15:38.900 --> 03:15:42.033
... are getting the same level of scrutiny that our school budget did, and to

03:15:42.066 --> 03:15:46.033
ensure that all of our investments are actually building public safety, trust,

03:15:46.066 --> 03:15:48.734
and well-being, and in alignment with our city's values. Thank you.

03:15:49.834 --> 03:15:51.133
Thank you very much.

03:15:52.900 --> 03:15:55.600
Additional public comment on the police budget.

03:15:59.500 --> 03:16:02.066
Hi, I'm James Laplante. I live on Broadway.

03:16:03.333 --> 03:16:07.166
I'm a small business owner and a resident of South Portland, and I'm here to

03:16:07.300 --> 03:16:11.133
ask you to reject the additional funding requested for the

03:16:11.133 --> 03:16:14.767
Flock camera systems that the city police currently

03:16:14.834 --> 03:16:15.367
utilize.

03:16:16.533 --> 03:16:20.300
I'd also like to request that the city end its contract with Flock in

03:16:20.333 --> 03:16:24.100
no undue terms, and remove these cameras from our neighborhood

03:16:24.166 --> 03:16:27.934
as soon as possible. While I appreciate the

03:16:27.967 --> 03:16:31.900
public safety services of our police department, I do not think the benefits of

03:16:31.934 --> 03:16:34.600
these camera systems outweigh their risks.

03:16:35.800 --> 03:16:39.667
Flock cameras are operated by private corporations that collect

03:16:39.767 --> 03:16:43.700
local data from these cameras to be used in a nationwide database.

03:16:45.033 --> 03:16:48.767
That database collects license plates and other

03:16:48.834 --> 03:16:50.767
information like facial recognition.

03:16:51.266 --> 03:16:53.266
Some cameras can even collect audio.

03:16:54.467 --> 03:16:58.233
These cameras have been proven to have security issues

03:16:58.800 --> 03:17:01.834
in the data that they collect and how they are shared.

03:17:01.867 --> 03:17:05.734
The data that is collect is being used in AI

03:17:05.767 --> 03:17:09.533
analytic systems that are controlled by a company called Palantir.

03:17:10.066 --> 03:17:10.533
Yeah.

03:17:10.600 --> 03:17:14.533
Palantir is funded by Peter Thiel, a tech billionaire who has

03:17:14.567 --> 03:17:18.467
been quoted as saying he no longer believes that freedom and democracy

03:17:18.533 --> 03:17:19.300
are compatible.

03:17:20.133 --> 03:17:23.800
Think about who is in charge of our data, our data that is going to these

03:17:23.834 --> 03:17:27.166
companies. We've been told not to worry about these cameras.

03:17:27.266 --> 03:17:31.066
They're only being used to track criminals. I'm a law-abiding citizen.

03:17:31.100 --> 03:17:34.266
I've never broken the law. I've barely gotten a speeding ticket.

03:17:34.934 --> 03:17:37.834
I take pride in being a contributing citizen to the city.

03:17:38.767 --> 03:17:41.433
I take pride in using my First Amendment rights.

03:17:41.634 --> 03:17:45.600
I attend peaceful protests in South Portland to raise my voice about

03:17:45.634 --> 03:17:48.500
matters exactly like this, and I am

03:17:48.567 --> 03:17:52.233
unapologetically anti-fascist.

03:17:52.333 --> 03:17:55.834
Last September, the White House issued a presidential memo expanding the

03:17:55.867 --> 03:17:58.333
definition of domestic terrorism to include

03:17:58.767 --> 03:17:59.867
anti-fascism.

03:18:01.266 --> 03:18:05.133
The Joint Task Force of Terrorism has been directed to investigate individuals or

03:18:05.233 --> 03:18:08.967
groups that hold these ideologies or participate in anti-fascist

03:18:09.033 --> 03:18:11.367
activities like peaceful protests.

03:18:12.300 --> 03:18:15.934
The data that is being collected by these cameras can be

03:18:16.066 --> 03:18:20.033
used to investigate peaceful protesters, and it will come from these

03:18:20.133 --> 03:18:22.133
Flock cameras in our neighborhood.

03:18:23.400 --> 03:18:26.233
It might not happen today, but it will happen.

03:18:27.066 --> 03:18:31.033
I do not trust that a corporation is in control of our private data

03:18:31.066 --> 03:18:31.400
or how-

03:18:31.400 --> 03:18:31.500
30 seconds

03:18:31.500 --> 03:18:34.967
... it will be used. I think that the risks of having these cameras in our

03:18:35.033 --> 03:18:38.900
neighborhoods outweighs the risks of our freedom, our privacy, and

03:18:39.033 --> 03:18:41.033
far outweigh the benefits of these police tools.

03:18:41.500 --> 03:18:45.367
South Portland did a fine job before they had these cameras were installed, and

03:18:45.433 --> 03:18:48.533
I'm confident they will continue to do a good job without them.

03:18:48.567 --> 03:18:51.934
Our crime rates are dropping. These cameras have nothing to do with it.

03:18:52.500 --> 03:18:56.467
Again, I ask this council to stop this contract, to reject

03:18:56.533 --> 03:18:59.367
it, and to get these cameras out of our city. Thank you.

03:19:00.533 --> 03:19:01.667
Thank you very much.

03:19:04.233 --> 03:19:04.700
Others?

03:19:06.634 --> 03:19:08.533
Carlton Parsons, South Portland.

03:19:10.734 --> 03:19:12.033
Good evening, Council.

03:19:13.567 --> 03:19:14.467
I was tasked,

03:19:15.367 --> 03:19:18.967
and at requested by a group of concerned citizens

03:19:19.567 --> 03:19:22.634
not to measure Flock by

03:19:23.934 --> 03:19:27.867
their human rights abuses, but simply by the quality of

03:19:27.934 --> 03:19:28.567
their company.

03:19:29.834 --> 03:19:33.834
So I did my research and used my analytics and research and academic

03:19:33.900 --> 03:19:37.634
tools to the test. Looking at the Flock research website,

03:19:37.967 --> 03:19:41.734
all of its research papers and case studies are paying customers,

03:19:42.166 --> 03:19:45.734
saying exactly what worked with no real methodology or

03:19:46.200 --> 03:19:47.233
statistical model.

03:19:48.367 --> 03:19:51.600
What started as a critique of Flock and their promises of

03:19:51.634 --> 03:19:55.133
improvements quickly became a larger analysis,

03:19:56.033 --> 03:19:59.900
covering a wide variety of white papers over

03:19:59.934 --> 03:20:01.100
the past five years.

03:20:02.133 --> 03:20:05.867
On the landmark Flock white paper itself, the study was

03:20:05.967 --> 03:20:08.967
authored and funded by Flock employees themselves.

03:20:09.834 --> 03:20:13.467
Only 74% of the total respondents made it to the final

03:20:13.567 --> 03:20:17.266
data. The self-reported attribution from

03:20:17.300 --> 03:20:18.367
those agencies,

03:20:19.166 --> 03:20:22.667
the authors themselves even concede that they cannot establish a

03:20:22.700 --> 03:20:23.700
causation

03:20:24.867 --> 03:20:28.266
in doing so, unlikely that their

03:20:28.333 --> 03:20:31.266
research will show that

03:20:32.500 --> 03:20:34.300
Flock has contributed.

03:20:35.634 --> 03:20:39.500
Including other research papers as well, an Atlantic

03:20:39.600 --> 03:20:42.867
City study, the most recent and rigorous form,

03:20:43.433 --> 03:20:47.033
found no reduction in overall violent crime rates, despite

03:20:47.133 --> 03:20:49.734
scanning every single vehicle entering the city.

03:20:51.634 --> 03:20:55.400
99% of scans by captured vehicles

03:20:55.500 --> 03:20:57.867
are connected with people with no crimes.

03:20:59.433 --> 03:21:03.400
Not only that, but there's documented real-world positive incidents that

03:21:03.433 --> 03:21:07.266
are plenty, including armed detentions in Aurora,

03:21:07.333 --> 03:21:10.233
California with a $1.9 million

03:21:10.266 --> 03:21:14.033
settlement, and CBS News verifying that more than a

03:21:14.133 --> 03:21:17.433
dozen such incidents have happened in a six-month investigation.

03:21:18.400 --> 03:21:21.867
I am more than happy to provide the City Council with a more

03:21:22.166 --> 03:21:26.000
thorough and provided research if you would allow me to do so.

03:21:26.567 --> 03:21:30.333
I am here to serve you and the citizens, and to provide a measured

03:21:30.467 --> 03:21:34.367
response in the effectiveness of Flock.It is up to us

03:21:34.433 --> 03:21:38.266
to decide whether these small improvements to

03:21:38.300 --> 03:21:41.734
crime are worth the risk to our community, and

03:21:41.800 --> 03:21:45.634
also to those relationships. The relationships

03:21:45.734 --> 03:21:49.100
between the community and the police ourselves

03:21:49.467 --> 03:21:53.300
all rely on those relationships. They

03:21:53.433 --> 03:21:56.667
provide those trusts to solve those more violent crimes.

03:21:57.667 --> 03:22:01.433
Those, and even within those studies, said that

03:22:01.467 --> 03:22:05.467
traditional policing every time outperforms Flock.

03:22:06.400 --> 03:22:10.200
So for us, it's important to look at the data and

03:22:10.266 --> 03:22:12.467
measure what is the most effective.

03:22:12.667 --> 03:22:16.467
And I'm happy to share those results with you by email. Thank you.

03:22:16.934 --> 03:22:18.233
Thank you very much.

03:22:21.634 --> 03:22:24.000
Hi. Kaylee Moore, Delbert Street.

03:22:25.800 --> 03:22:28.734
I'd like to just reflect on kind of two recent experiences.

03:22:29.000 --> 03:22:32.767
Um, the ICE surge in January, which many of us were

03:22:32.834 --> 03:22:35.834
stepping up to help our neighbors, and we now know many of our neighbors were not

03:22:35.867 --> 03:22:38.066
criminals even though they were detained.

03:22:39.467 --> 03:22:43.300
In talking with other cities that have gone through similar experiences,

03:22:43.367 --> 03:22:46.467
we were told when we were driving into these communities we should be covering our

03:22:46.467 --> 03:22:49.667
license plates with snow, we should be turning our phones off.

03:22:51.133 --> 03:22:53.934
I don't think I personally thought that moving to South Berlin, those would be

03:22:54.000 --> 03:22:57.333
things that I would be considering, and it is really deeply upsetting.

03:22:58.433 --> 03:23:02.133
I'm sure we also all saw the video of the Portland

03:23:02.233 --> 03:23:05.467
resident who was told she's now in a database when she was just

03:23:05.767 --> 03:23:06.967
existing in her town.

03:23:09.000 --> 03:23:12.467
As we discussed, and as our police chief discussed, behavioral health is actually

03:23:12.500 --> 03:23:16.367
what will stop crime. I used to be a social worker. I deeply believe that.

03:23:16.767 --> 03:23:18.700
It was really cool to hear about your program.

03:23:20.000 --> 03:23:21.000
Those to me seem

03:23:23.100 --> 03:23:26.934
like much better things to be supporting and funding than something that will

03:23:27.000 --> 03:23:30.533
be tracking us, not because we have a police department that is

03:23:30.567 --> 03:23:34.233
behaving inappropriately, but because we live in a country that I think we really

03:23:34.266 --> 03:23:36.800
can't trust other people with our data right now.

03:23:37.767 --> 03:23:41.266
So I just would like to ask that you stop the contract,

03:23:42.467 --> 03:23:44.634
that you move that funding to something more productive.

03:23:44.667 --> 03:23:47.533
We just sat and listened to what is happening within our town,

03:23:48.533 --> 03:23:51.667
and that we focus on the things that we know will keep us safe, like proactive and

03:23:51.734 --> 03:23:54.634
preventative mental health services and other things.

03:23:55.834 --> 03:23:59.000
So I think just to reiterate, everyone else here spoke so well.

03:24:00.367 --> 03:24:04.333
It is so important to me that I can feel safe and that everybody feels

03:24:04.400 --> 03:24:08.333
safe, and the cameras are in certain locations, and they are targeting certain

03:24:08.400 --> 03:24:12.300
people, and that is just not, I think, what we all want for our

03:24:12.367 --> 03:24:14.667
town and our community. So thank you very much.

03:24:15.100 --> 03:24:15.166
Thank you.

03:24:15.200 --> 03:24:17.934
And I don't know if I'm allowed to give my extra time to somebody else, but

03:24:20.533 --> 03:24:21.834
Thank you for being generous.

03:24:23.200 --> 03:24:26.734
Anyone else? Yes. So it looks like we have at least two people.

03:24:27.533 --> 03:24:27.934
Come on.

03:24:28.033 --> 03:24:30.133
I think we have two after me, if I saw correctly.

03:24:31.166 --> 03:24:32.867
Willis Duvall, Ocean View Avenue.

03:24:34.433 --> 03:24:37.133
I'd like to echo everything that everyone else said.

03:24:37.300 --> 03:24:39.567
I didn't go to ranger school. I'm not a data analyst.

03:24:40.000 --> 03:24:41.567
But I do have two kids that I'm raising here.

03:24:43.567 --> 03:24:46.734
And there were two flanks that kind of stuck out to me in this conversation.

03:24:46.767 --> 03:24:50.667
Before I came in, I was watching the video feed, which I think we're very fortunate

03:24:50.700 --> 03:24:51.100
to have.

03:24:52.667 --> 03:24:54.200
And the cost of an ed tech came up.

03:24:55.166 --> 03:24:57.233
It's roughly double the cost of this Flock program.

03:24:58.200 --> 03:25:01.700
So the idea that we would cut half an FTE from an already cash-strapped school

03:25:01.734 --> 03:25:05.567
department to fund clearly extra-constitutional data surveillance,

03:25:09.000 --> 03:25:12.734
it's inexplicable to me, and I mean this in the most civil way

03:25:12.734 --> 03:25:16.333
possible, it will have severe electoral consequences for anyone who supports it.

03:25:17.100 --> 03:25:18.066
Probably legal too.

03:25:19.133 --> 03:25:21.767
But this is an issue that everyone I've talked to, as soon as they hear about it,

03:25:22.000 --> 03:25:22.567
is outraged.

03:25:23.433 --> 03:25:27.000
They don't believe that this council, that I think is generally fairly well viewed,

03:25:27.367 --> 03:25:28.000
would support it.

03:25:29.467 --> 03:25:33.266
And after a hellish experience with federal law

03:25:33.300 --> 03:25:36.433
enforcement in this community less than three months ago,

03:25:38.000 --> 03:25:41.700
our police department is asking for more money for the exact tools that

03:25:41.734 --> 03:25:43.700
enabled that kind of encroachment on our rights.

03:25:46.800 --> 03:25:50.367
I think we have very good reason to be skeptical of exactly how cozy

03:25:50.634 --> 03:25:53.066
local enforcement actually is with those authorities,

03:25:54.400 --> 03:25:55.533
as the Press Herald discovered.

03:25:56.367 --> 03:25:58.767
And we can talk about procedure all we wish,

03:25:59.834 --> 03:26:01.000
but this is something that has

03:26:02.100 --> 03:26:05.300
very, very, very little public support, and for good reason, legally,

03:26:05.900 --> 03:26:06.333
morally,

03:26:07.667 --> 03:26:10.367
and financially. And if we're talking about a cash-strapped community, this is

03:26:10.433 --> 03:26:12.066
absolutely not something we should be spending money on.

03:26:12.100 --> 03:26:15.634
And frankly, if it were free, we couldn't get paid enough to accept it.

03:26:17.367 --> 03:26:20.367
I too have a small daughter who lives in this community.

03:26:20.900 --> 03:26:21.667
She lives in my house.

03:26:24.333 --> 03:26:28.000
And she's very curious, she's very talkative, and she asked a lot of

03:26:28.033 --> 03:26:30.834
questions when ICE was here. She asked why people were standing on corners

03:26:30.900 --> 03:26:34.166
protesting. She asked why there were very,

03:26:34.433 --> 03:26:38.333
very interesting people walking around her school in orange vests to make

03:26:38.367 --> 03:26:42.333
sure the kids were safe. She asked why they're still walking around her

03:26:42.333 --> 03:26:44.100
school to make sure the kids are safe.

03:26:45.000 --> 03:26:46.133
I can't really tell them it's that

03:26:47.133 --> 03:26:50.867
we want our kids to stay safe, and I can't tell them it's because there is a

03:26:50.934 --> 03:26:54.367
federal government that has very little interest in enforcing its own rules to

03:26:54.400 --> 03:26:56.500
protect us as citizens, and the fact that this,

03:26:57.533 --> 03:26:59.900
I would like to think, enclave of moral and-

03:27:00.767 --> 03:27:01.066
30 seconds

03:27:01.066 --> 03:27:01.867
... legal virtue,

03:27:02.767 --> 03:27:04.567
would even consider something like this,

03:27:05.734 --> 03:27:09.333
again, I mean this civilly and peacefully, there will be severe, severe electoral

03:27:09.367 --> 03:27:10.133
consequences.

03:27:11.166 --> 03:27:13.133
And it is morally unforgivable.

03:27:14.166 --> 03:27:17.667
And this is to say nothing of the clear racial disparities that clearly

03:27:17.700 --> 03:27:20.033
disadvantage the people who are not represented in this room.

03:27:20.567 --> 03:27:22.967
Certainly not on the council, and that's no fault of your own, but it ought to be

03:27:23.033 --> 03:27:26.867
considered. Thank you for your time, thank you for this marathon meeting, and thank

03:27:26.867 --> 03:27:27.367
you for hearing me.

03:27:28.467 --> 03:27:30.734
Thank you very much. Next.

03:27:32.066 --> 03:27:32.667
Thank you.

03:27:35.767 --> 03:27:38.800
Hi, I'm Shelby Leighton. I live on Stanley Street.

03:27:40.767 --> 03:27:44.634
We have gone through a lot of pain in the last

03:27:44.700 --> 03:27:48.533
few weeks about raising the school budget

03:27:48.567 --> 03:27:51.400
by 6 or 7%. And

03:27:51.533 --> 03:27:53.867
it has

03:27:53.934 --> 03:27:57.500
involved 80 people losing their jobs,

03:27:57.867 --> 03:27:59.000
a school closing,

03:28:00.734 --> 03:28:03.467
all sorts of really, really, really hard decisions.

03:28:04.100 --> 03:28:07.133
And so I really want us to take that same

03:28:07.133 --> 03:28:08.567
energy that we

03:28:09.634 --> 03:28:13.333
looked at the school budget with and look at the police budget

03:28:13.400 --> 03:28:17.166
request to increase by 6.5% with that same energy.

03:28:17.934 --> 03:28:21.900
And I want us to think about why each of the line

03:28:21.967 --> 03:28:25.834
items in this police budget is more necessary to the

03:28:25.834 --> 03:28:29.834
safety of our community and more important to us and

03:28:29.867 --> 03:28:33.467
all of our neighbors than the people who are teaching our children,

03:28:34.000 --> 03:28:37.567
and who are feeding our children, and who are doing all the important work in our

03:28:37.634 --> 03:28:40.133
schools. And I think that I heard

03:28:42.133 --> 03:28:46.100
some really great things that are going on in the police department budget,

03:28:46.166 --> 03:28:49.767
like the SoPo Unite program, like the behavioral health liaisons,

03:28:50.634 --> 03:28:54.567
that should be funded and that do meet that criteria, but there are other things in

03:28:54.600 --> 03:28:58.533
the budget that do not meet that criteria, and sort of the lowest hanging fruit

03:28:58.600 --> 03:29:01.734
of all is this Flock contract. And

03:29:03.734 --> 03:29:07.433
Flock's business model is to create a nationwide network of

03:29:07.533 --> 03:29:11.533
cameras that surveils all of us anywhere we go and can be

03:29:11.567 --> 03:29:14.133
searched by any police department anywhere.

03:29:16.033 --> 03:29:19.467
I have not heard from anyone, from the police chief,

03:29:20.100 --> 03:29:23.867
from the city manager, from the council, what safeguards we have in

03:29:23.900 --> 03:29:27.767
place to stop that from happening when that is the entire

03:29:27.834 --> 03:29:29.634
reason that Flock exists.

03:29:30.433 --> 03:29:33.033
It's not clear that anyone here

03:29:33.667 --> 03:29:36.233
knows what Flock is doing with our data.

03:29:37.033 --> 03:29:39.567
And no matter what safeguards we put in place,

03:29:40.433 --> 03:29:44.166
Flock will always find loopholes to exploit to

03:29:44.166 --> 03:29:48.166
ensure that it can do what it was created to do, which is

03:29:48.233 --> 03:29:52.166
create a nationwide surveillance network that it can sell

03:29:52.300 --> 03:29:53.033
for profit.

03:29:54.734 --> 03:29:58.634
I think other folks have already mentioned that there's examples,

03:29:58.934 --> 03:30:02.600
for example, in California, which has a strong law against sharing

03:30:02.667 --> 03:30:06.367
ALPR data outside of the state or with federal officials.

03:30:06.667 --> 03:30:07.834
There's been numerous examples-

03:30:07.900 --> 03:30:07.900
30 seconds

03:30:07.934 --> 03:30:11.767
... of Flock nonetheless doing that without the permission of police departments

03:30:12.200 --> 03:30:15.467
and in violation of state law.

03:30:16.667 --> 03:30:20.500
And I just have no confidence that they're not going to do that here

03:30:20.967 --> 03:30:22.100
no matter what we do.

03:30:24.333 --> 03:30:28.000
So I think we should not spend any more money on Flock

03:30:28.233 --> 03:30:32.233
until we know that it is keeping us safe and not putting us at

03:30:32.266 --> 03:30:33.333
risk. Thank you.

03:30:34.233 --> 03:30:35.433
Thank you very much.

03:30:50.066 --> 03:30:52.500
Councilor Steph Steinbrink, Cottage Road.

03:30:53.567 --> 03:30:57.467
I commend and admire and will try not simply to

03:30:57.533 --> 03:30:59.967
echo the speakers who come before me.

03:31:00.934 --> 03:31:03.133
Someone referred to this as a marathon meeting.

03:31:03.433 --> 03:31:07.266
I do not want to do more than my three minutes to contribute to that.

03:31:10.467 --> 03:31:14.266
And I think we would be happy either to have you just deny the

03:31:14.467 --> 03:31:18.100
54 grand that's to be designated to

03:31:18.367 --> 03:31:22.233
Flock or to say, "Well, we'll table that, and we'll have a community-wide

03:31:22.266 --> 03:31:25.934
discussion about this where everybody can talk," and we can really

03:31:26.033 --> 03:31:27.834
air the concerns here.

03:31:29.100 --> 03:31:32.266
Fine either way with that, just so you know what I think we're after.

03:31:32.300 --> 03:31:35.567
We didn't get together, so I'm not sure what my colleagues are about

03:31:35.634 --> 03:31:36.300
here.

03:31:38.133 --> 03:31:41.834
So these ALPR cameras,

03:31:41.900 --> 03:31:45.333
especially these Flock cameras, they're in about 5,000

03:31:45.367 --> 03:31:49.100
communities. There are about 80,000 of them in the United States

03:31:49.133 --> 03:31:49.567
alone.

03:31:51.700 --> 03:31:55.667
They scan 20 billion license plates

03:31:55.834 --> 03:31:56.367
in a month.

03:31:57.834 --> 03:32:00.567
So we're talking about a big enterprise here, and we

03:32:00.734 --> 03:32:04.467
have, as you've heard, kind of flimsy

03:32:04.567 --> 03:32:08.033
guarantees about how all that data is going to be used.

03:32:08.033 --> 03:32:11.967
But we do know this, so they call their present cameras Sparrow and

03:32:12.000 --> 03:32:15.600
Falcon, but they've got one called Condor that's on the way.

03:32:16.200 --> 03:32:19.634
And Condor will be able to read people's faces as they pass.

03:32:20.233 --> 03:32:23.967
The technology now already has a thing

03:32:24.033 --> 03:32:25.367
called vehicle

03:32:26.166 --> 03:32:30.033
fingerprint capability, and that means that it isn't just

03:32:30.033 --> 03:32:33.800
capturing your license plate, it's also capturing the things that make

03:32:33.900 --> 03:32:37.367
your car unique among all the automobiles on the American

03:32:37.433 --> 03:32:41.333
highways. That means any dent in your car, any stickers on your

03:32:41.400 --> 03:32:43.266
car, any kinds of

03:32:44.467 --> 03:32:48.333
racks or canoes or whatever you have on your car, all that gets recorded, too.

03:32:48.533 --> 03:32:51.066
So this isn't just happenstancial.

03:32:52.133 --> 03:32:55.934
I want to say, I come from a generation where my relationship with the police

03:32:55.934 --> 03:32:57.867
was at best, and I think

03:32:58.834 --> 03:33:01.000
my friends' relationship, troubled.

03:33:01.734 --> 03:33:05.066
And it's taken me a long time, and it's taken me living in this

03:33:05.100 --> 03:33:08.834
community to have some sense about the kind of

03:33:08.900 --> 03:33:12.834
coordination and collaboration and even admiration that I can feel

03:33:12.867 --> 03:33:16.533
for the police department. So this is nothing about

03:33:16.700 --> 03:33:20.567
them that I particularly question, but I do think

03:33:20.634 --> 03:33:23.634
the wisdom of undertaking this kind of program,

03:33:24.433 --> 03:33:24.967
especially-

03:33:25.133 --> 03:33:25.700
30 seconds

03:33:27.533 --> 03:33:28.934
... with its inherent dangers,

03:33:29.734 --> 03:33:32.266
especially in the political

03:33:33.300 --> 03:33:37.266
atmosphere that we live in now, all of this just seems to me

03:33:37.367 --> 03:33:37.734
to be

03:33:38.667 --> 03:33:42.233
... clearly mistaken, and I would urge you not to support this

03:33:42.266 --> 03:33:45.634
part of what the police department is asking

03:33:45.634 --> 03:33:47.066
for. Thank you.

03:33:52.500 --> 03:33:53.467
Thank you. Sorry.

03:33:54.967 --> 03:33:58.600
Hey, everybody. Sam Anderson. I live on Dawson Street over by Cash

03:33:58.700 --> 03:33:59.000
Corner.

03:33:59.967 --> 03:34:03.400
I don't have anything prepared. I have a three-month-year-old baby at home, and I

03:34:03.467 --> 03:34:07.100
work a lot, so time is precious. And echoing that,

03:34:07.233 --> 03:34:11.066
won't echo many of the other things that my colleagues here have said, all of

03:34:11.100 --> 03:34:13.000
which I agree with regarding this program.

03:34:13.767 --> 03:34:15.266
Like I said, I live on Dawson Street.

03:34:15.367 --> 03:34:16.000
I work

03:34:17.433 --> 03:34:20.000
between Darling Ave near the mall, and then on

03:34:21.066 --> 03:34:24.800
Bradley Drive in Westbrook. So on an average weekday, I'm

03:34:24.834 --> 03:34:27.600
clocked by these cameras 10 times plus.

03:34:29.333 --> 03:34:30.533
And the thing I want to highlight,

03:34:31.567 --> 03:34:34.600
outside of all the moral concerns with the company and

03:34:35.100 --> 03:34:36.433
surveillance state...

03:34:38.066 --> 03:34:39.266
is device security.

03:34:40.200 --> 03:34:43.867
These cameras have been proven to have serious security

03:34:43.900 --> 03:34:46.967
exploits that Flock has repeatedly lied about and denied.

03:34:47.867 --> 03:34:51.600
And basically, anybody with some pretty basic computer

03:34:51.700 --> 03:34:55.634
skills and readily accessible equipment can access

03:34:55.667 --> 03:34:56.467
these cameras

03:34:57.500 --> 03:34:59.967
without passwords, without security.

03:35:00.400 --> 03:35:03.834
And some of these cameras can capture full motion video,

03:35:03.900 --> 03:35:07.300
audio. I could borrow the stuff at work to do it tomorrow.

03:35:07.400 --> 03:35:10.200
I won't, because that's illegal. But- ...

03:35:12.467 --> 03:35:16.000
I think that that's a serious concern on top of all this other stuff.

03:35:17.033 --> 03:35:21.000
And I think that in addition to ending this

03:35:21.066 --> 03:35:24.700
program and removing all of the cameras, I think we should have legal protection

03:35:24.767 --> 03:35:28.567
against things like this being set up in our community in the future. Thank you.

03:35:30.700 --> 03:35:34.467
Thank you very much. Is there anyone else with a comment about the

03:35:34.533 --> 03:35:35.567
police budget?

03:35:37.567 --> 03:35:39.433
Thank you. Oh, you got two folks.

03:35:40.367 --> 03:35:40.500
Well,

03:35:41.300 --> 03:35:43.567
Jeff spoke, so I have to speak also.

03:35:45.166 --> 03:35:45.767
No, you don't.

03:35:48.066 --> 03:35:48.233
Council.

03:35:48.266 --> 03:35:48.967
Good one, Richie.

03:35:50.467 --> 03:35:54.066
Don Pine, Beach Street. I do not have prepared

03:35:54.300 --> 03:35:56.500
remarks. I've just been listening to people.

03:35:58.834 --> 03:36:02.800
I'm an old software guy, and I thought I retired, but a lot of

03:36:02.867 --> 03:36:05.166
the software work has followed me.

03:36:06.500 --> 03:36:10.300
And so a part of me just says, "Look, this is a technology

03:36:10.634 --> 03:36:10.900
that

03:36:12.233 --> 03:36:16.066
we'll be contending with from now on." The artificial

03:36:16.133 --> 03:36:19.500
intelligence capabilities of camera

03:36:19.600 --> 03:36:23.066
recognition, computer recognition are here to stay.

03:36:24.367 --> 03:36:25.634
That's part of me.

03:36:26.800 --> 03:36:30.200
I think one of the things that really upset me

03:36:30.700 --> 03:36:32.767
in hearing people's opinions here,

03:36:33.967 --> 03:36:36.266
was that even when laws are passed,

03:36:37.133 --> 03:36:40.767
this company, Flock, violates the law anyway.

03:36:41.266 --> 03:36:44.233
That even when communities speak and states speak and say,

03:36:45.266 --> 03:36:49.200
"Here's the boundary. You cannot use this technology

03:36:49.200 --> 03:36:52.767
to go over this line. Stay on this side of the line, okay.

03:36:53.300 --> 03:36:56.967
But go over the line, that's illegal." Apparently,

03:36:57.300 --> 03:36:59.867
Flock has been violating those laws.

03:37:00.767 --> 03:37:04.700
That's deeply troubling. So what I would like to say

03:37:04.800 --> 03:37:08.367
to the city when I take all these

03:37:08.667 --> 03:37:09.100
different

03:37:10.900 --> 03:37:14.500
thoughts and dimensions that run through this and think of them

03:37:14.600 --> 03:37:15.000
together,

03:37:15.967 --> 03:37:19.667
this is an issue that this city must understand.

03:37:20.000 --> 03:37:23.800
We need to understand this. We

03:37:23.934 --> 03:37:27.800
take issues like sea level rise. I don't know, is Julie

03:37:27.867 --> 03:37:30.200
Rosenbach still here? There she is.

03:37:30.500 --> 03:37:34.300
She knows about sea level rise because

03:37:34.800 --> 03:37:38.767
she's had to. We take issues like the extreme storms that have

03:37:38.800 --> 03:37:42.667
come. Do you guys know what direction they come from when they wipe out

03:37:43.200 --> 03:37:46.467
Willard Beach? They come from the southeast. We know that now.

03:37:46.567 --> 03:37:50.533
That's an issue that we as a community have had to

03:37:50.667 --> 03:37:51.900
come to understand.

03:37:54.767 --> 03:37:58.500
My neighbors have convinced me there's a serious problem here and a

03:37:58.600 --> 03:38:02.567
serious issue with this new technology that, again,

03:38:02.700 --> 03:38:05.300
based on my background as a software guy,

03:38:06.400 --> 03:38:08.200
we know this technology's coming.

03:38:09.266 --> 03:38:13.066
There are obvious legal problems, illegal search-

03:38:13.100 --> 03:38:13.367
30 seconds

03:38:13.400 --> 03:38:13.767
... and seizure,

03:38:15.300 --> 03:38:19.200
the need for warrants. There are obvious national,

03:38:19.300 --> 03:38:21.066
state legal issues here. So,

03:38:21.900 --> 03:38:25.767
the only thing I really want to say here

03:38:25.900 --> 03:38:29.500
is just like the sea level rise, just like the storms,

03:38:30.033 --> 03:38:31.867
just like the budget shortfalls,

03:38:32.867 --> 03:38:36.600
this is an issue that this city is going to have to come to

03:38:36.667 --> 03:38:37.867
understand. Thank you.

03:38:38.867 --> 03:38:39.867
Thank you very much.

03:38:40.734 --> 03:38:43.100
I thought there was one more person. Yes. Thank you.

03:38:49.200 --> 03:38:50.934
Hi, everyone. My name is Julia.

03:38:51.767 --> 03:38:54.934
If I sound out of breath, it's because I am four months pregnant, and I am.

03:38:57.600 --> 03:39:01.200
I moved to South Portland two years ago, and I actually am an

03:39:01.266 --> 03:39:04.900
employee of Flock. They did not ask me to come here. I came here on my own accord.

03:39:06.400 --> 03:39:09.700
I'm here because I'm local, and I care about this community being safe,

03:39:10.033 --> 03:39:13.634
and I also once had a lot of questions and

03:39:13.700 --> 03:39:14.533
misinformation.

03:39:16.300 --> 03:39:20.200
I want to start with the fact that Flock has helped solve over one million crimes,

03:39:20.467 --> 03:39:24.066
and that the cost of crime per household in South Portland, according to

03:39:24.100 --> 03:39:27.667
crimegrade.org, is over $700 a

03:39:27.800 --> 03:39:30.467
year per household. This was from 2025.

03:39:32.066 --> 03:39:36.000
I understand that you want facts, and I would like them, too, so I'm

03:39:36.033 --> 03:39:38.567
going to address some common myths that circulate around Flock.

03:39:39.567 --> 03:39:42.567
Flock license plate readers do not track people.

03:39:42.567 --> 03:39:46.066
They do not know your name, they do not know where you live, and they do not follow

03:39:46.133 --> 03:39:49.967
you aroundFloc software has built-in safety guards

03:39:50.500 --> 03:39:54.400
that work to enable proper usage. For example, all

03:39:54.467 --> 03:39:57.033
searches in Floc must be tied to an offense type.

03:39:57.634 --> 03:39:58.266
There are no

03:39:59.600 --> 03:40:00.567
random searches.

03:40:02.433 --> 03:40:05.467
We are not owned by Palantir, nor does he have access to our

03:40:05.500 --> 03:40:09.133
data. All of our searches in the system are

03:40:09.166 --> 03:40:13.100
audited and tracked. Certain searches are blocked in states where bans and

03:40:13.200 --> 03:40:16.700
policies ban sensitive material like abortion and immigration.

03:40:18.066 --> 03:40:21.834
We have tools in place to check to see if atypical usage is

03:40:21.867 --> 03:40:22.300
happening,

03:40:23.200 --> 03:40:26.967
like our audit assistance tool that flags behavior that we think warrants a

03:40:27.000 --> 03:40:30.667
closer look. This enables your police chief or Floc

03:40:30.734 --> 03:40:32.867
admin to monitor the usage more often.

03:40:34.300 --> 03:40:38.066
I also want to call out that Floc does not have a contract with ICE or DHS.

03:40:38.600 --> 03:40:40.900
They do not have backdoor access to Floc.

03:40:43.800 --> 03:40:46.967
Your police team, and I'm going to work with them personally on

03:40:47.066 --> 03:40:50.634
this, can have a transparency portal that is available to the

03:40:50.667 --> 03:40:51.100
public.

03:40:52.266 --> 03:40:56.133
This portal will show how Floc is used, its usage

03:40:56.200 --> 03:40:56.800
metrics,

03:40:57.600 --> 03:41:00.800
and access details like who your police are sharing data with, if

03:41:01.467 --> 03:41:01.867
anyone.

03:41:03.233 --> 03:41:06.300
I would also like to call out that there is no auto-sharing in Floc.

03:41:07.166 --> 03:41:09.667
There is no national or federal auto-sharing.

03:41:09.800 --> 03:41:13.266
If your police department chooses to share data with another

03:41:13.300 --> 03:41:17.066
department or would like to have another department's data shared with them, it

03:41:17.200 --> 03:41:18.567
has to be a two-way agreement.

03:41:19.767 --> 03:41:22.100
This is also something that could be shown on the transparency portal.

03:41:22.100 --> 03:41:22.433
30 seconds.

03:41:23.767 --> 03:41:27.600
I would also like to say that South Portland Police own 100% of the data collected

03:41:27.667 --> 03:41:31.600
here. Floc does not own any data, does not have access to data unless you

03:41:31.767 --> 03:41:32.834
grant it to it,

03:41:34.066 --> 03:41:36.934
and we have never sold or shared your data with anyone.

03:41:37.533 --> 03:41:39.467
The agencies have complete control.

03:41:41.567 --> 03:41:45.066
Finally, I'd like to say that Floc products actually reduce bias in

03:41:45.166 --> 03:41:47.133
policing with objective evidence.

03:41:47.967 --> 03:41:50.233
I think it's fair to ask questions, and I continue to.

03:41:50.433 --> 03:41:50.433
Time.

03:41:50.467 --> 03:41:54.266
I continue to encourage you to. I'm here, and your police chief are here to answer

03:41:54.300 --> 03:41:56.000
questions you have. Thank you.

03:41:56.066 --> 03:41:57.200
Thank you very much.

03:41:57.266 --> 03:41:59.667
Yeah, who are you? You don't work for the government.

03:41:59.700 --> 03:42:00.734
No, I don't work for the government.

03:42:00.734 --> 03:42:01.300
Yeah. What's your name?

03:42:01.767 --> 03:42:02.367
Sorry, my name's-

03:42:02.367 --> 03:42:03.467
Wait. Guys.

03:42:04.033 --> 03:42:04.500
Whoa.

03:42:04.767 --> 03:42:05.400
She said-

03:42:05.533 --> 03:42:06.200
We all have to do that, right? We all have to.

03:42:06.200 --> 03:42:09.400
She didn't say what her name was.

03:42:10.266 --> 03:42:12.967
Julia, did you say your last name?

03:42:13.200 --> 03:42:14.567
No, my last name is Ferreri.

03:42:14.867 --> 03:42:16.200
Well, you can talk to me.

03:42:16.266 --> 03:42:16.500
Sorry.

03:42:17.400 --> 03:42:20.967
So I'm sorry, I thought I didn't hear your last name.

03:42:21.066 --> 03:42:22.700
I did hear your first name, Julia.

03:42:22.800 --> 03:42:23.600
Julia Ferreri.

03:42:24.667 --> 03:42:28.200
Ferreri. Nobody else had spelled their name, so we'll take it just like we hear it.

03:42:29.200 --> 03:42:29.767
And-

03:42:29.867 --> 03:42:30.767
I'll spell my last name.

03:42:31.500 --> 03:42:31.500
Fine.

03:42:33.800 --> 03:42:35.600
You're Sam Anders? No, you're not.

03:42:36.266 --> 03:42:37.467
So, I-

03:42:37.867 --> 03:42:38.500
We're all good.

03:42:38.734 --> 03:42:41.867
Julia, I think you're finished your comment. Thank you very much.

03:42:44.200 --> 03:42:44.934
You're Willis.

03:42:45.500 --> 03:42:47.066
DeLatt. D-L-A-T.

03:42:47.133 --> 03:42:51.000
All right, everybody, now we know who everybody's name is, and if there is

03:42:51.100 --> 03:42:54.767
any doubt, we can watch it on our video, but I think we've been

03:42:54.834 --> 03:42:56.500
keeping track. I have anyway.

03:42:57.767 --> 03:43:01.667
Thank you everyone. Is there anyone else who has a comment about the police

03:43:01.700 --> 03:43:05.367
budget? And remember, they did talk more than just about the Floc

03:43:05.500 --> 03:43:09.000
cameras, so if there is anything related to the police budget.

03:43:10.667 --> 03:43:14.600
Okay, it doesn't look like that. So we're going to close public comment,

03:43:15.767 --> 03:43:19.333
and truly appreciate all of the comments. Thank you.

03:43:21.266 --> 03:43:24.000
And we now have a little council discussion.

03:43:24.166 --> 03:43:28.100
Oh, we do have questions that the city manager has answers to, and I have a

03:43:28.166 --> 03:43:31.967
feeling that we also will have questions that might require a little

03:43:32.000 --> 03:43:35.667
bit more time to try to get some answers to, but maybe not.

03:43:36.200 --> 03:43:38.934
Well, I only have two questions that I had, so I don't know.

03:43:39.400 --> 03:43:42.567
But the first one was why did the council know about this?

03:43:42.667 --> 03:43:44.000
Why wasn't there any announcement?

03:43:44.066 --> 03:43:46.967
So this, in October of 2024, on October 8th,

03:43:47.767 --> 03:43:51.567
the city council, during a publicly noticed meeting with agenda materials publicly

03:43:51.600 --> 03:43:55.367
available, accepted a JAG grant to purchase specifically Floc

03:43:55.500 --> 03:43:58.867
cameras. So it was very clear in the agenda materials. It wasn't a secret.

03:43:58.900 --> 03:44:02.500
It wasn't hidden. This isn't a grant the PD got without anyone's

03:44:02.567 --> 03:44:05.066
knowledge. It was public, transparent.

03:44:05.467 --> 03:44:08.934
The Sanford decision was made a year later, so it doesn't quite line up with when

03:44:08.934 --> 03:44:12.834
the council accepted the grant versus September of 2025, when

03:44:12.900 --> 03:44:16.266
Sanford had their debate and discussion. So there's a year gap there.

03:44:17.500 --> 03:44:20.967
So those times don't really add up.

03:44:21.367 --> 03:44:24.266
I don't know if other communities announce when they're putting cameras up.

03:44:24.367 --> 03:44:28.100
If we didn't and others did, then maybe that's something we fell

03:44:28.133 --> 03:44:31.767
short on. But anyway, there was a public process.

03:44:32.467 --> 03:44:35.967
The safeguards that are in place, it sounds like maybe the council will put this

03:44:36.100 --> 03:44:37.433
into the workshop

03:44:38.266 --> 03:44:39.734
for further discussion on the 12th.

03:44:40.300 --> 03:44:43.567
I think that would be great, and I hope everyone shows up for that that did

03:44:43.600 --> 03:44:47.233
tonight, maybe even more so that we can have a fuller conversation because it's

03:44:47.266 --> 03:44:50.100
important to understand all the risks

03:44:50.967 --> 03:44:54.200
with Floc. I've looked into it quite a bit because a lot of concern has been

03:44:54.233 --> 03:44:54.734
brought up.

03:44:56.200 --> 03:45:00.066
There's some things that I think are worth talking about, worth the public

03:45:00.100 --> 03:45:01.800
understanding, and making sure the council

03:45:02.967 --> 03:45:06.867
understands it as well and makes decisions based on the facts

03:45:06.900 --> 03:45:10.500
of the matter and can that way determine whether or not the money should

03:45:10.500 --> 03:45:13.800
be included in the budget or not. So I think we're at that

03:45:13.834 --> 03:45:17.700
time. We can talk more, but generally, the safeguards include state law, city

03:45:17.834 --> 03:45:21.600
policy, access logs, the fact that we haven't

03:45:21.667 --> 03:45:25.567
enabled sharing with ICE, and our policy

03:45:25.600 --> 03:45:27.200
says that we won't, for example,

03:45:28.734 --> 03:45:30.333
as well are some of the safeguards.

03:45:30.400 --> 03:45:33.967
But they're good questions, and I think it does warrant a fuller discussion.

03:45:35.967 --> 03:45:38.433
Okay, and I have, I think, one more question.

03:45:39.233 --> 03:45:43.033
Mr. Parsons asked if he could send research that he's done to the

03:45:43.100 --> 03:45:46.200
council. Anyone can email the council at any time.

03:45:47.500 --> 03:45:48.734
So that is a

03:45:48.800 --> 03:45:52.800
yesUm,

03:45:53.066 --> 03:45:53.400
okay.

03:45:54.700 --> 03:45:55.233
Misha.

03:45:56.066 --> 03:45:57.300
I mean, Councilor Pride. Sorry.

03:45:57.600 --> 03:45:59.367
No, it's all right. It's getting late.

03:46:01.433 --> 03:46:05.333
One thing I didn't say before is I do want to point out all the staff who

03:46:05.400 --> 03:46:09.066
are still here, and I thank you, and I hope that the residents

03:46:09.100 --> 03:46:12.700
understand. It's 10:25.

03:46:12.767 --> 03:46:16.700
Do any of you go into work at 10:25, after working a full

03:46:16.734 --> 03:46:17.233
day of work?

03:46:18.066 --> 03:46:18.700
Probably not many,

03:46:19.900 --> 03:46:22.133
so thank you, staff, for still being here.

03:46:23.233 --> 03:46:26.300
I'm sure some people do, but it's not very common.

03:46:26.600 --> 03:46:28.934
Anyway, thank you, staff, for still being here.

03:46:29.033 --> 03:46:32.000
I will just make two requests for the parking lot.

03:46:32.300 --> 03:46:34.000
One would be the Flock cameras.

03:46:35.500 --> 03:46:39.367
And I ask that along with whatever

03:46:39.433 --> 03:46:40.133
information

03:46:41.300 --> 03:46:45.200
you and the chief can provide, Mr. City Manager, that we

03:46:45.266 --> 03:46:49.066
also get an analysis of the contract with Flock from our corporation

03:46:49.200 --> 03:46:52.233
counsel to give us a better idea of,

03:46:52.900 --> 03:46:56.100
legally, what they can and can't

03:46:56.166 --> 03:46:59.967
do with our data. So that, and then the

03:47:00.100 --> 03:47:02.400
second thing I'd like to put on the

03:47:05.133 --> 03:47:08.400
parking lot is the SoCo United position-

03:47:09.533 --> 03:47:10.133
Here's the mic

03:47:10.166 --> 03:47:10.734
... for funding.

03:47:12.300 --> 03:47:13.767
Where'd funding come from?

03:47:13.867 --> 03:47:14.834
It would be taxes.

03:47:15.000 --> 03:47:15.166
Okay.

03:47:16.166 --> 03:47:19.000
Unless we find something else in the meantime. But for now, it's taxes.

03:47:21.433 --> 03:47:21.600
Okay.

03:47:21.634 --> 03:47:21.634
Okay.

03:47:21.634 --> 03:47:22.133
Madam Mayor?

03:47:22.734 --> 03:47:23.033
Yes.

03:47:23.100 --> 03:47:26.500
I'd also request that if Julia is available that night,

03:47:27.100 --> 03:47:30.433
because she is working with the police department, if you wouldn't mind coming back

03:47:30.500 --> 03:47:32.166
for the follow-up discussion.

03:47:33.066 --> 03:47:33.767
Sure. When is that?

03:47:34.900 --> 03:47:36.400
Do we have a date?

03:47:36.433 --> 03:47:36.834
May 12th.

03:47:37.367 --> 03:47:41.200
I would like to request that if that is part...

03:47:43.000 --> 03:47:45.100
We heard from

03:47:45.934 --> 03:47:48.500
this person named Julia as a

03:47:49.767 --> 03:47:53.467
making public comment, but if this is actually

03:47:53.533 --> 03:47:57.066
someone who is a consultant with the police department, shouldn't we get that

03:47:57.133 --> 03:47:57.934
information?

03:47:59.200 --> 03:48:00.767
I'm not aware.

03:48:01.600 --> 03:48:03.000
Is this a consultant for the department?

03:48:03.033 --> 03:48:03.333
I'm not-

03:48:03.367 --> 03:48:06.033
Can I speak a little more on what my position is, just to clarify?

03:48:06.934 --> 03:48:09.834
Well, actually, Chief, I'd like to hear from you, thank you.

03:48:10.500 --> 03:48:12.700
Is Julia working with you?

03:48:13.800 --> 03:48:14.734
She will be.

03:48:20.066 --> 03:48:21.066
Dan Hearn, police chief.

03:48:22.200 --> 03:48:24.834
I met Julia as I walked in the door. She said, "Hi, Chief.

03:48:24.834 --> 03:48:27.834
I'm Julia." I said, "Julia, how are you?" "I work with Flock." Great.

03:48:28.033 --> 03:48:30.500
Great to see you. She took it upon herself to be here.

03:48:30.600 --> 03:48:31.400
She's a resident,

03:48:32.233 --> 03:48:36.133
and I applaud her for that. She is working with us,

03:48:36.300 --> 03:48:38.767
as I learned when we had our conversation downstairs.

03:48:39.333 --> 03:48:40.667
We've had a bunch of different people.

03:48:42.500 --> 03:48:44.467
I'm going to stop there, because I could talk for-

03:48:44.634 --> 03:48:45.333
All right. So just-

03:48:45.900 --> 03:48:46.634
... four hours

03:48:46.634 --> 03:48:47.834
... all I'm asking is-

03:48:48.800 --> 03:48:49.600
I will have people-

03:48:49.634 --> 03:48:52.634
Julia is not known to you as the person who sells you Flock.

03:48:53.967 --> 03:48:55.967
You've already established that.

03:48:56.166 --> 03:48:56.300
She's-

03:48:56.367 --> 03:48:56.600
Correct

03:48:56.634 --> 03:48:58.600
... a resident who sells for them.

03:48:58.634 --> 03:49:02.233
We worked with someone else when we purchased these cameras.

03:49:02.333 --> 03:49:02.433
Okay.

03:49:02.500 --> 03:49:05.133
A different representative from Flock, but she represents Flock.

03:49:05.367 --> 03:49:05.667
All right. So I think we've got that, see.

03:49:05.700 --> 03:49:07.700
Yeah, I mean, she wouldn't be part of our presentation.

03:49:07.767 --> 03:49:09.967
She'd be here if council has questions, but we'd let her know.

03:49:10.000 --> 03:49:13.467
