04:12:22.066 --> 04:12:25.100
I'm just going to do really quick because I know Carl really wants to go tonight.

04:12:25.800 --> 04:12:26.400
Our biggest

04:12:27.800 --> 04:12:31.767
increase is overtime, but that's because of union wages that have

04:12:31.834 --> 04:12:35.667
been negotiated. Equipment rental's up quite a

04:12:35.700 --> 04:12:38.600
bit, but that's our winter plowing contractors.

04:12:39.600 --> 04:12:42.467
Can you explain that real quick, the on-call?

04:12:42.634 --> 04:12:44.333
I think that's important for the council understanding.

04:12:44.367 --> 04:12:48.333
So, every time that we put this out to bid, every three years,

04:12:48.700 --> 04:12:52.600
we get pretty much one vendor. It's really tough to get contractors

04:12:52.667 --> 04:12:53.066
out there,

04:12:54.066 --> 04:12:56.066
because they're tied up at other municipalities.

04:12:56.133 --> 04:12:58.700
For example, Scarborough has Dearborn.

04:12:58.867 --> 04:13:01.367
We had Keenan and Gorham Sand,

04:13:02.266 --> 04:13:05.200
and then other municipalities have other contractors.

04:13:05.600 --> 04:13:09.233
So there's not much out there for plow

04:13:09.300 --> 04:13:13.266
contractors. Basically, how it works is if we have a smaller

04:13:13.333 --> 04:13:16.700
storm, we do that in-house. That's why you'll see some times where people say it

04:13:16.734 --> 04:13:17.767
takes a little bit longer

04:13:18.867 --> 04:13:20.567
or we haven't been around to plow their road.

04:13:20.600 --> 04:13:24.367
It's because we're trying to fill up those nine spots with our drivers.

04:13:24.834 --> 04:13:28.700
So we're struggling, so there's routes that don't get touched until the guys

04:13:28.734 --> 04:13:31.900
finish their dedicated route, then they work into the other

04:13:31.967 --> 04:13:35.667
routes. And we do that to cut costs, because we obviously couldn't

04:13:35.767 --> 04:13:37.600
fund contractors every single storm.

04:13:38.233 --> 04:13:42.200
So we try to use what we have wisely and use it for

04:13:42.266 --> 04:13:43.133
larger storms.

04:13:44.800 --> 04:13:48.600
And what we do is we have to give them a two-hour call, so two-hour heads up.

04:13:48.667 --> 04:13:52.634
So we call them in advance, they come in within two hours, and then they start

04:13:52.667 --> 04:13:53.100
plowing.

04:13:54.066 --> 04:13:57.867
So there's a rate per hour for the loaders, which is pretty much about

04:13:57.867 --> 04:14:01.767
$200 an hour, $215 an hour, and then the grader

04:14:01.867 --> 04:14:05.433
is $300 an hour. So you pay them per hour, and that includes their

04:14:05.467 --> 04:14:07.700
equipment, the fuel, the labor, everything.

04:14:08.533 --> 04:14:10.367
And then we also pay winter storage.

04:14:10.467 --> 04:14:14.300
So for every piece of equipment that we retain by them, we have to pay a monthly

04:14:14.433 --> 04:14:16.800
storage to make sure that we're guaranteed the equipment.

04:14:17.266 --> 04:14:20.767
If not, then the equipment then moves, and then they have to haul the equipment

04:14:20.867 --> 04:14:21.400
back in.

04:14:22.767 --> 04:14:25.767
So during the storm, we wouldn't have the equipment readily available.

04:14:26.867 --> 04:14:28.600
So we're not getting much bidders on it.

04:14:28.634 --> 04:14:30.900
It is out there right now for bid, so

04:14:31.967 --> 04:14:34.834
hopefully we'll get more people interested, but we'll see.

04:14:35.634 --> 04:14:36.834
So that's the increase there.

04:14:38.033 --> 04:14:41.867
Construction supplies increase is just because the salt per ton is

04:14:41.900 --> 04:14:45.800
very expensive. We do use salt on all our main roads, and then we

04:14:45.900 --> 04:14:48.634
also mix in 30% salt with our sand.

04:14:50.333 --> 04:14:54.033
Our largest

04:14:54.100 --> 04:14:56.300
increase is solid waste and recycling.

04:14:57.066 --> 04:15:00.900
That is the EcoMain fees have gone up, Casella curbside collection has gone

04:15:01.000 --> 04:15:04.767
up. A lot more interest in our household hazardous waste event,

04:15:05.200 --> 04:15:08.300
so that has quite a bit more participants and higher volume, which is

04:15:08.333 --> 04:15:11.800
great. The Garbage to Garden increased,

04:15:13.066 --> 04:15:16.734
and then also contamination fees, tipping fees through EcoMain has

04:15:16.800 --> 04:15:17.467
increased.

04:15:19.266 --> 04:15:21.433
And then that is it for our operating.

04:15:21.467 --> 04:15:25.100
And as for capital, we are requesting two

04:15:25.133 --> 04:15:27.367
single-axle trucks, and those are plow trucks.

04:15:28.367 --> 04:15:31.166
Those are replacing a 2002 and a 2009,

04:15:32.100 --> 04:15:34.567
and that still leaves us with old fleet.

04:15:34.967 --> 04:15:38.367
We still have other 2002s, 2007s,

04:15:38.400 --> 04:15:41.533
four 2008s, 2011.

04:15:43.333 --> 04:15:45.066
So we have a lot of aging fleet.

04:15:46.367 --> 04:15:50.233
We asked for a compact excavator, and that's just we don't have one now, and that

04:15:50.300 --> 04:15:52.266
saves on us renting the equipment.

04:15:52.567 --> 04:15:55.100
It's also more efficient to remove sidewalks.

04:15:56.500 --> 04:16:00.433
A skid steer, that is for pretty much everything in the summer, and

04:16:00.500 --> 04:16:02.567
that is a 2005 we're replacing.

04:16:03.433 --> 04:16:06.967
We're looking at replacing the sign shop truck. That's currently a 2012.

04:16:07.133 --> 04:16:11.100
And because we are in the urban compact, we oversee all of the

04:16:11.266 --> 04:16:14.900
state roads. So all of the overhead wires, the span

04:16:14.967 --> 04:16:18.900
wires-Signage, all of that is us, and we do not have

04:16:18.967 --> 04:16:21.433
a truck capable of being able to do that.

04:16:22.500 --> 04:16:26.400
Parks does have a bucket truck, but they use it quite often during

04:16:26.433 --> 04:16:30.200
the season to maintain trees. So this would be outfitted with a

04:16:30.266 --> 04:16:33.800
bucket, and that would allow us to replace spin wires, back plates

04:16:33.834 --> 04:16:36.367
on traffic signals, clean the

04:16:37.333 --> 04:16:40.700
video detection cameras for the actual signals.

04:16:41.634 --> 04:16:44.967
It'll be outfitted with a puller to actually replace larger signs.

04:16:46.433 --> 04:16:48.367
And then we also have on there a street opening truck.

04:16:48.500 --> 04:16:51.033
That is funded by street opening permits.

04:16:51.200 --> 04:16:53.567
That's currently replacing a 2014

04:16:54.500 --> 04:16:54.867
car.

04:16:56.233 --> 04:16:59.800
And then we have a local match for our Crockett's Corner design.

04:17:00.200 --> 04:17:03.000
That is something that came out of the Safe Streets for All assessment.

04:17:03.834 --> 04:17:07.500
Crockett's Corner is a high-crash location. It has a history of safety concerns.

04:17:07.834 --> 04:17:09.500
It's a $30,000 match,

04:17:10.367 --> 04:17:14.200
and then we get a federal grant for $270,000, and that is the complete

