04:23:31.600 --> 04:23:33.400
different areas this year.

04:23:34.700 --> 04:23:37.967
There's about $10,000 to flush heat loops.

04:23:38.300 --> 04:23:41.300
So a lot of these buildings have a closed loop in them where they run the heat.

04:23:42.500 --> 04:23:46.266
In that loop, the water in it gets stagnant after

04:23:46.333 --> 04:23:50.233
years. So basically, the city has never flushed any of these loops in

04:23:50.266 --> 04:23:54.133
the buildings that we own. We've got new buildings like MSF and Cash

04:23:54.266 --> 04:23:57.967
Corner that have these loops, and so I want to make sure that we're doing this now,

04:23:58.000 --> 04:24:00.800
and it should be done every five years or so.

04:24:01.166 --> 04:24:03.033
So we put that in as a five-year

04:24:05.467 --> 04:24:09.200
preventative maintenance. There's also some other things that were never in here in

04:24:09.233 --> 04:24:12.967
the preventive maintenance. There's a five-year sprinkler inspection.

04:24:13.333 --> 04:24:16.800
Every five years, an internal inspection needs to be done with sprinkler systems,

04:24:16.900 --> 04:24:20.500
so they drain the system. They run cameras down it to look at the

04:24:20.500 --> 04:24:22.300
interior of the pipe, so on and so forth.

04:24:22.967 --> 04:24:24.767
That's never been done in the city before either.

04:24:24.800 --> 04:24:28.700
I want to make sure we're getting that into our new buildings, Cash Corner,

04:24:29.166 --> 04:24:32.900
Municipal Service Facilities, and this building here needs it as

04:24:32.967 --> 04:24:36.967
