04:51:14.767 --> 04:51:18.500
year-round and play an integral role in winter operations when they're

04:51:18.533 --> 04:51:20.500
not working at the course.

04:51:22.400 --> 04:51:24.433
Currently, we have two full-time employees at the course.

04:51:26.567 --> 04:51:30.500
One has a split allocation that is 40% paid for

04:51:30.567 --> 04:51:34.367
by Parks and 60% paid for by the golf course, and the other is completely

04:51:34.500 --> 04:51:38.200
paid by the Parks budget. Since the golf course is in a position to be

04:51:38.233 --> 04:51:41.734
self-sustaining, funding 100% of the foreperson

04:51:41.800 --> 04:51:45.000
position utilizing user fees and still having the

04:51:45.200 --> 04:51:49.066
40/60 split employee would allow us to maintain the current staffing

04:51:49.166 --> 04:51:52.800
levels at the course and continue to provide a high level of service to the

04:51:52.900 --> 04:51:56.867
community. And by shifting the financial burden from Parks

04:51:57.000 --> 04:52:00.800
to the golf course for that position, the savings to the Parks operating budget

04:52:00.834 --> 04:52:04.767
would allow us to add an additional full-time position to our budget at no

04:52:04.834 --> 04:52:08.133
added expense. We're just taking that person and we're shifting it over to

04:52:08.734 --> 04:52:10.600
our revenue-generating machine.

